[LIMEN][WS]: message: {:prompt=>"these are good points... i tried to introduce a better mapping of PID to aerolastic effects but just introduced new instabilities ... i think my tendencies have been working but are not fully developed. i have been working on a new flapping parameter called ferocity in another project for rp2040. ferocity is an extra parameter that may apply on downstroke or upstroke, this part of the wave is mathematically transformed into a more and more near rectangular wave, which is starting to move earlier and stays more at higher speed. generally more ferocity is more thrust, but a bit in efficient. ferocity on downstroke adds therefore more pitch up and ferocity on upstroke adds more elevator down effect from the pulse. this kind of wave shaping that is regarding up and downstroke separately is key for efficient stabilization and you can see in my code i have already been doing that. please check my new improvement of the flapping algorithm and introduce them in this project and further think about how we can combine and enhance the stabilization techniques and find a new formula. you may create a task for this", :record=>true, :attachments=>[]}
