efined(USE_GYRO_SPI_MPU6000) || defined(USE_GYRO_SPI_MPU6500)  || defined(USE_GYRO_SPI_ICM20689)\n#define PID_PROCESS_DENOM_DEFAULT       4\n#else\n#define PID_PROCESS_DENOM_DEFAULT       2\n#endif\n", :range=>[85, 110], :execution_time=>0.007}, :args=>{:path=>"src/main/flight/pid.c", :range=>[86, 110]}, :execution_time=>0.008}, {:content=>"I now have the full picture of both systems. Let me inscribe what I've learned and create the task."}, {:id=>"call_00_NCsmRGy8YoBaUJ05EHSW5457", :name=>"remember", :result=>{:ok=>true, :execution_time=>0.003}, :args=>{:content=>"Gralha Azul (RP2040) ferocity formula in formaDoBaterDasAsas(): shapedWave = tanh(ferocity * sin(θ)) / tanh(ferocity). Ferocity per channel: downstroke (CH7, 1.0-8.0), upstroke (CH8, 1.0-8.0), with linear blend zone ±0.1 rad at zero crossing. Low ferocity → pure sine; high ferocity → near square wave (earlier movement, longer at extreme). Wave always normalized to [-1,+1]. Servo rate limiting in glide: ferocity controls transition speed. Constants: FEROCIDADE_MINIMA_PADRAO=1.0, FEROCIDADE_MAXIMA_PADRAO=8.0, EPSILON_FORMA_BATER_PADRAO=1e-6, LIMITE_FORMA_BATER_PADRAO=1.0.", :tags=>["ferocity", "code", "formula", "gralha-azul"], :links=>["/Users/d/Desktop/HOI_KOSMOI/paraeksperiment/Arduino/libraries/o-grande-codigo-da-gralha-azul/src/GralhaAzul.h", "/Users/d/Desktop/HOI_KOSMOI/paraeksperiment/Arduino/libraries/o-grande-codigo-da-gralha-azul/src/GralhaAzul_Padraos.h"]}, :execution_time=>0.004}, {:content=>""}, {:id=>"call_00_vONzB541vwDB6kCLQZOt7708", :name=>"create_task", :result=>{"ok"=>true, "id"=>1, :title=>"Port Ferocity Wave-Shaping into OrniFlight & Unify with ONDAS", :plan=>"## Goal\nPort the ferocity wave-shaping algorithm from the Gralha Azul RP2040 project into OrniFlight's flight controller, and unify it with the existing ONDAS stabilization to create a combined formula where ferocity-distorted wing kinematics naturally sharpen the ONDAS PID attenuation window.\n\n## The Ferocity Formula (from Gralha Azul)\n```\nshapedWave = tanh(ferocity * sin(θ)) / tanh(ferocity)\n```\n- Separate ferocity for downstroke (sinθ > 0) and upstroke (sinθ < 0)\n- Linear blend zone at ±0.1 rad around zero crossing\n- ferocity range: 1.0 (pure sine) to 8.0 (near square wave)\n- Wave always normalized to [-1, +1]\n\n## Combined ONDAS+Ferocity Formula\n```\nshapedWave = tanh(F * sin(θ)) / tanh(F)   where F = ferocity_down or ferocity_up\nondasAttenuation = -|shapedWave| + 0.5\n```\nHigher ferocity → wave stays longer near ±1 → narrower ONDAS window at midstroke → aerodynamically correct PID gating.\n\n## Steps\n\n### Step 1: Add ferocity parameters to servoConfig_t in servos.h\n- Add `ornithopter_ferocity_downstroke` (int8_t, range 1-100 mapped to 1.0-8.0)\n- Add `ornithopter_ferocity_upstroke` (int8_t, range 1-100 mapped to 1.0-8.0)\n- Add defaults (e.g. 12 → ferocity ~1.0, pure sine)\n\n### Step 2: Add CLI settings entries in settings.c\n- `ornithopter_ferocity_downstroke` and `ornithopter_ferocity_upstroke`\n- Following existing pattern of ornithopter parameters\n\n### Step 3: Add PG defaults in servos.c or wherever servoConfig PG reset is defined\n\n### Step 4: Implement ferocity wave shaping in pid.c\n- Add `shapedFlappingSinusoid` global alongside existing `flappingSinusoid`\n- Implement `applyFerocityWaveShaping(float sinTheta, float ferocityDown, float ferocityUp)` \n- Call it from `calculateFlappingFromThrottle()` after computing `sin(theta)`\n- Map int8_t parameters to float ferocity (1.0-8.0 range)\n\n### Step 5: Update ONDAS to use shaped wave\n- Change `ondasAttenuation = -fabs(shapedFlappingSinusoid) + 0.5`\n- Update `ondasAttenuationDerivative` to use shaped wave derivative\n- Update `flappingDerivative` to use shaped wave\n- Update `ornithopterFlapping = shapedFlappingSinusoid * flappingAmplitude`\n\n### Step 6: Update servo output path\n- `applyFlappingToServos()` already uses `ornithopterFlapping`, which will now carry the shaped wave\n\n### Step 7: Update ONDAS.md documentation with the unified formula\n\n### Step 8: Store project notes in Mnemosyne", :workflow_type=>"full", :parent_task_id=>nil, :execution_time=>0.003}, :args=>{:title=>"Port Ferocity Wave-Shaping into OrniFlight & Unify with ONDAS", :plan=>"## Goal\nPort the ferocity wave-shaping algorithm from the Gralha Azul RP2040 project into OrniFlight's flight controller, and unify it with the existing ONDAS stabilization to create a combined formula where ferocity-distorted wing kinematics naturally sharpen the ONDAS PID attenuation window.\n\n## The Ferocity Formula (from Gralha Azul)\n```\nshapedWave = tanh(ferocity * sin(θ)) / tanh(ferocity)\n```\n- Separate ferocity for downstroke (sinθ > 0) and upstroke (sinθ < 0)\n- Linear blend zone at ±0.1 rad around zero crossing\n- ferocity range: 1.0 (pure sine) to 8.0 (near square wave)\n- Wave always normalized to [-1, +1]\n\n## Combined ONDAS+Ferocity Formula\n```\nshapedWave = tanh(F * sin(θ)) / tanh(F)   where F = ferocity_down or ferocity_up\nondasAttenuation = -|shapedWave| + 0.5\n```\nHigher ferocity → wave stays longer near ±1 → narrower ONDAS window at midstroke → aerodynamically correct PID gating.\n\n## Steps\n\n### Step 1: Add ferocity parameters to servoConfig_t in servos.h\n- Add `ornithopter_ferocity_downstroke` (int8_t, range 1-100 mapped to 1.0-8.0)\n- Add `ornithopter_ferocity_upstroke` (int8_t, range 1-100 mapped to 1.0-8.0)\n- Add defaults (e.g. 12 → ferocity ~1.0, pure sine)\n\n### Step 2: Add CLI settings entries in settings.c\n- `ornithopter_ferocity_downstroke` and `ornithopter_ferocity_upstroke`\n- Following existing pattern of ornithopter parameters\n\n### Step 3: Add PG defaults in servos.c or wherever servoConfig PG reset is defined\n\n### Step 4: Implement ferocity wave shaping in pid.c\n- Add `shapedFlappingSinusoid` global alongside existing `flappingSinusoid`\n- Implement `applyFerocityWaveShaping(float sinTheta, float ferocityDown, float ferocityUp)` \n- Call it from `calculateFlappingFromThrottle()` after computing `sin(theta)`\n- Map int8_t parameters to float ferocity (1.0-8.0 range)\n\n### Step 5: Update ONDAS to use shaped wave\n- Change `ondasAttenuation = -fabs(shapedFlappingSinusoid) + 0.5`\n- Update `ondasAttenuationDerivative` to use shaped wave derivative\n- Update `flappingDerivative` to use shaped wave\n- Update `ornithopterFlapping = shapedFlappingSinusoid * flappingAmplitude`\n\n### Step 6: Update servo output path\n- `applyFlappingToServos()` already uses `ornithopterFlapping`, which will now carry the shaped wave\n\n### Step 7: Update ONDAS.md documentation with the unified formula\n\n### Step 8: Store project notes in Mnemosyne"}, :execution_time=>0.005}, {:content=>"The task is inscribed. Now let me execute. First, let me find the PG reset for servoConfig and the control rate profile defaults:"}, {:id=>"call_00_Al4pXAB1Bm3ObJZxFMx03351", :name=>"run_command", :result=>{:ok=>true, :exit_status=>0, :result=>"Command output: 61:void pgResetFn_servoConfig(servoConfig_t *servoConfig) {\n\n(exit 0)", :execution_time=>0.126}, :args=>{:cmd=>"grep -n 'PG_RESET.*servoConfig\\|pgResetFn.*servoConfig\\|\\.flap_base_frequency\\|\\.ornithopter_glide\\|\\.ondas_gain\\|\\.aeroelastic' src/main/flight/servos.c | head -20"}, :execution_time=>0.126}, {:id=>"call_01_HtOmVJxPPdpVOGS4VH4K8772", :name=>"run_command", :result=>{:ok=>true, :exit_status=>0, :result=>"Command output: src/main/flight/servos.c:61:void pgResetFn_servoConfig(servoConfig_t *servoConfig) {\n\n(exit 0)", :execution_time=>1.58}, :args=>{:cmd=>"grep -rn 'PG_RESET.*servoConfig\\|pgReset.*servoConfig' src/main/ | head -10"}, :execution_time=>1.58}, {:content=>""}, {:id=>"call_00_Ekl6YFsTbXs6wrnxGSGv8567", :name=>"read_file", :result=>{:content=>"#include \"rx/rx.h\"\n\nextern mixerMode_e currentMixerMode;\n\nPG_REGISTER_WITH_RESET_FN(servoConfig_t, servoConfig, PG_SERVO_CONFIG, 0);\n\nvoid pgResetFn_servoConfig(servoConfig_t *servoConfig) {\n    servoConfig->dev.servoCenterPulse = 1500