er, and unify it with the existing ONDAS stabilization to create a combined formula where ferocity-distorted wing kinematics naturally sharpen the ONDAS PID attenuation window.\n\n## The Ferocity Formula (from Gralha Azul)\n```\nshapedWave = tanh(ferocity * sin(θ)) / tanh(ferocity)\n```\n- Separate ferocity for downstroke (sinθ > 0) and upstroke (sinθ < 0)\n- Linear blend zone at ±0.1 rad around zero crossing\n- ferocity range: 1.0 (pure sine) to 8.0 (near square wave)\n- Wave always normalized to [-1, +1]\n\n## Combined ONDAS+Ferocity Formula\n```\nshapedWave = tanh(F * sin(θ)) / tanh(F)   where F = ferocity_down or ferocity_up\nondasAttenuation = -|shapedWave| + 0.5\n```\nHigher ferocity → wave stays longer near ±1 → narrower ONDAS window at midstroke → aerodynamically correct PID gating.\n\n## Steps\n\n### Step 1: Add ferocity parameters to servoConfig_t in servos.h ✅\n### Step 2: Add CLI settings entries in settings.c ✅\n### Step 3: Add PG defaults in servos.c ✅\n### Step 4: Implement ferocity wave shaping in pid.c ✅\n### Step 5: Update ONDAS to use shaped wave ✅\n### Step 6: Update servo output path ✅ (automatic via ornithopterFlapping)\n### Step 7: Update ONDAS.md documentation ✅\n### Step 8: Store project notes in Mnemosyne ✅\n\n## Files Modified\n- src/main/flight/servos.h — added ornithopter_ferocity_downstroke/upstroke\n- src/main/flight/servos.c — PG defaults (12)\n- src/main/cli/settings.c — CLI entries\n- src/main/flight/pid.c — core ferocity wave shaping + ONDAS integration\n- ONDAS.md — unified documentation\n\n## Build Status\nAll source files compile successfully. Linker error ('mixers' undefined) is pre-existing and unrelated."}, :execution_time=>0.005}, {:content=>"Let me clean up the older ONDAS notes since the architecture has evolved:"}, {:id=>"call_00_VRnmDZ1JqL0FyVy5cNws1448", :name=>"recall_notes", :result=>{:notes=>[{:id=>4, :content=>"ONDAS full architecture: Second-order ODE solver (calculateFlappingFromThrottle) at pid.c:585-619 drives f