nvoid applyPhaseShift(float pitchError) {\n    theta += (currentControlRateProfile->phase_shift_scale * 0.000000001) \n      * fabs(pitchError) * flappingDerivative * (1.0 + pitchError * 0.1);\n}\n\n", :range=>[556, 575], :execution_time=>0.01}, :args=>{:path=>"src/main/flight/pid.c", :range=>[557, 575]}, :execution_time=>0.01}, {:content=>""}, {:id=>"call_00_TSsoIxuUyheYCDKurEyQ3480", :name=>"read_file", :result=>{:content=>"\n\n\nvoid calculateFlappingFromThrottle(float rc_throttle) {\n    tcommand = (rc_throttle - 480.0)  \n        * ((1.0 / (0.1 * (float)servoConfig()->flap_base_frequency)) \n            + ((float)(currentControlRateProfile->flap_speed_modificator - 1500) \n                * 0.000725));\n\n    omegadot = k0 * tcommand - k2 * omega;\n    thetadot = omega;\n\n    theta = theta + omega * dT;\n    omega = omega + omegadot * dT;\n\n    if (rc_throttle > GLIDE_MODE_THRESHOLD) {\n        //flappingSinusoid = (sin(x) - pow_approx(sin(x), 3) / 3) * 1.5;//squared\n        flappingSinusoid = sin(theta);\n        flappingSinusoid2 = flappingSinusoid * flappingSinusoid;\n        flappingCosinusoid = cos(theta);\n        // P term filter\n        // ondasAttenuation = -pow_approx(1.0 - flappingSinusoid2, 4) + 1.0;\n        // ondasAttenuationDerivative = 8.0 * pow_approx(1.0 - flappingSinusoid2, 3) * flappingSinusoid * flappingCosinusoid;\n        // ondasAttenuation = 2 * flappingSinusoid * flappingCosinusoid;\n        ondasAttenuation = -fabs(flappingSinusoid) + 0.5;\n        ondasAttenuationDerivative = flappingCosinusoid * flappingCosinusoid - flappingSinusoid2;\n\n        // used for countering of errorRate\n        flappingDerivative = thetadot * flappingCosinusoid;\n        // used for I term scaling\n        normalizedFlappingIntegral = flappingDerivative / tcommand + 1.0;\n        ornithopterFlapping = flappingSinusoid * flappingAmplitude;\n    }\n    else {\n        flappingDerivative = 0.0;\n        ornithopterFlapping = 0.0;\n        ondasAttenuation = 0.5;\n        ondasAttenuationDerivative = 1.0;\n        normalizedFlappingIntegral = 1.0;\n    }\n}\n\n\nfloat aerolastic_Kp_scaling = 0.01;\nfloat aerolastic_Ki_scaling = 0.005;\n", :range=>[581, 625], :execution_time=>0.013}, :args=>{:path=>"src/main/flight/pid.c", :range=>[582, 625]}, :execution_time=>0.013}, {:content=>""}, {:id=>"call_00_ibXSCfXhJvYbHEfW3Lbh4977", :name=>"run_command", :result=>{:ok=>true, :exit_status=>0, :result=>"Command output: 93:static FAST_RAM_ZERO_INIT float ondasAttenuation;\n94:static FAST_RAM_ZERO_INIT float ondasAttenuationDerivative;\n603:        // ondasAttenuation = -pow_approx(1.0 - flappingSinusoid2, 4) + 1.0;\n604:        // ondasAttenuationDerivative = 8.0 * pow_approx(1.0 - flappingSinusoid2, 3) * flappingSinusoid * flappingCosinusoid;\n605:        // ondasAttenuation = 2 * flappingSinusoid * flappingCosinusoid;\n606:        ondasAttenuation = -fabs(flappingSinusoid) + 0.5;\n607:        ondasAttenuationDerivative = flappingCosinusoid * flappingCosinusoid - flappingSinusoid2;\n618:        ondasAttenuation = 0.5;\n619:        ondasAttenuationDerivative = 1.0;\n1476:            errorRate *= (1.0 + ((ondasAttenuation - 0.5) * (float)servoConfig()-&gt;ondas_gain * 0.1));\n1477:            // errorRate *= (1.0 - (ondasAttenuation * sqrtf(throttle_) * (float)servoConfig()-&gt;ondas_gain * 0.01));\n1480:            // errorRate -= normalizedFlappingIntegral * (float)servoConfig()-&gt;ondas_gain2 * 0.1;\n1499:            axis == FD_PITCH &amp;&amp; servoConfig()-&gt;ondas_gain2 != 0 ? (normalizedFlappingIntegral * servoConfig()-&gt;ondas_gain2 * 0.1) : 1.0;\n1521:        // -----calculate D component // ondasAttenuationDerivative\n1524:          // const float deltaOndasFlapFactor = axis == FD_PITCH ? 1.0 + ((ondasAttenuationDerivative) * (float)servoConfig()-&gt;ondas_gain3 * 0.1) : 1.0;\n1525:          const float deltaOndasFlapFactor = axis == FD_PITCH ? 1.0 + ((ondasAttenuationDerivative - 0.5) * (float)servoConfig()-&gt;ondas_gain3 * 0.1) : 1.0;\n\n(exit 0)", :execution_time=>0.095}, :args=>{:cmd=>"grep -n 'ondasAttenuation\\|ondas_gain' src/main/flight/pid.c | head -30"}, :execution_time=>0.095}, {:content=>"Now the core — implementing ferocity wave shaping and unifying with ONDAS. Let me replace the `calculateFlappingFromThrottle` function:"}, {:id=>"call_00_hInuIGAjcpiRSDL1eoJP8184", :name=>"patch_file", :result=>{:ok=>true, :execution_time=>2.494}, :args=>{:diff=>"<<<<<<< SEARCH\n:start_line:583\n-------\nvoid calculateFlappingFromThrottle(float rc_throttle) {\n    tcommand = (rc_throttle - 480.0)  \n        * ((1.0 / (0.1 * (float)servoConfig()->flap_base_frequency)) \n            + ((float)(currentControlRateProfile->flap_speed_modificator - 1500) \n                * 0.000725));\n\n    omegadot = k0 * tcommand - k2 * omega;\n    thetadot = omega;\n\n    theta = theta + omega * dT;\n    omega = omega + omegadot * dT;\n\n    if (rc_throttle > GLIDE_MODE_THRESHOLD) {\n        //flappingSinusoid = (sin(x) - pow_approx(sin(x), 3) / 3) * 1.5;//squared\n        flappingSinusoid = sin(theta);\n        flappingSinusoid2 = flappingSinusoid * flappingSinusoid;\n        flappingCosinusoid = cos(theta);\n        // P term filter\n        // ondasAttenuation = -pow_approx(1.0 - flappingSinusoid2, 4) + 1.0;\n        // ondasAttenuationDerivative = 8.0 * pow_approx(1.0 - flappingSinusoid2, 3) * flappingSinusoid * flappingCosinusoid;\n        // ondasAttenuation = 2 * flappingSinusoid * flappingCosinusoid;\n        ondasAttenuation = -fabs(flappingSinusoid) + 0.5;\n        ondasAttenuationDerivative = flappingCosinusoid * flappingCosinusoid - flappingSinusoid2;\n\n        // used for countering of errorRate\n        flappingDerivative = thetadot * flappingCosinusoid;\n        // used for I term scaling\n        normalizedFlappingIntegral = flappingDerivative / tcommand + 1.0;\n        ornithopterFlapping = flappingSinusoid * flappingAmplitude;\n    }\n    else {\n        flappingDerivative = 0.0;\n        ornithopterFlapping = 0.0;\n        ondasAttenuation = 0.5;\n        ondasAttenuationDerivative = 1.0;\n        normalizedFlappingIntegral = 1.0;\n    }\n}\n=======\nstatic inline float ferocityParamToFloat(int8_t param) {\n    return 1.0f + ((float)(param - 1) * 7.0f / 99.0f);\n}\n\nstatic void applyFerocityWaveShaping(float sinTheta) {\n    float fDown = ferocityParamToFloat(servoConfig()->ornithopter_ferocity_downstroke);\n    float fUp   = ferocityParamToFloat(servoConfig()->ornithopter_ferocity_upstroke);\n\n    float ferocity;\n    if (sinTheta >= 0.1f) {\n        ferocity = fDown;\n    } else if (sinTheta <= -0.1f) {\n        ferocity = fUp;\n    } else {\n        float t = (sinTheta + 0.1f) * 5.0f; // map [-0.1,0.1] → [0,1]\n        ferocity = fUp + (fDown - fUp) * t;\n    }\n\n    float tanhF = tanhf(ferocity);\n    if (fabsf(tanhF) < 1e-6f) {\n        shapedFlappingSinusoid = sinTheta;\n        return;\n    }\n\n    shapedFlappingSinusoid = tanhf(ferocity * sinTheta) / tanhF;\n\n    if (shapedFlappingSinusoid >  1.0f) shapedFlappingSinusoid =  1.0f;\n    if (shapedFlappingSinusoid < -1.0f) shapedFlappingSinusoid = -1.0f;\n}\n\nvoid calculateFlappingFromThrottle(float rc_throttle) {\n    tcommand = (rc_throttle - 480.0)  \n        * ((1.0 / (0.1 * (float)servoConfig()->flap_base_frequency)) \n            + ((float)(currentControlRateProfile->flap_speed_modificator - 1500) \n                * 0.000725));\n\n    omegadot = k0 * tcommand - k2 * omega;\n    thetadot = omega;\n\n    theta = theta + omega * dT;\n    omega = omega + omegadot * dT;\n\n    if (rc_throttle > GLIDE_MODE_THRESHOLD) {\n        flappingSinusoid = sin(theta);\n        flappingSinusoid2 = flappingSinusoid * flappingSinusoid;\n        flappingCosinusoid = cos(theta);\n\n        // Ferocity wave shaping: transform sin(θ) → tanh(F·sinθ)/tanh(F)\n        applyFerocityWaveShaping(flappingSinusoid);\n\n        // ONDAS attenuation uses the ferocity-shaped wave\n        // |shapedWave| ≈ 0 at midstroke → attenuation = +0.5 (PID amplified)\n        // |shapedWave| ≈ 1 at extremity → attenuation = -0.5 (PID suppressed)\n        // Higher ferocity → sharper transitions → narrower, more precise PID window\n        ondasAttenuation = -fabsf(shapedFlappingSinusoid) + 0.5f;\n\n        // Derivative smoothed via cos(2θ): captures rate-of-change of flapping\n        ondasAttenuationDerivative = flappingCosinusoid * flappingCosinusoid - flappingSinusoid2;\n\n        // Shaped derivative: d/dt[shapedWave] for error-rate countering\n        float fDown = ferocityParamToFloat(servoConfig()->ornithopter_ferocity_downstroke);\n        float fUp   = ferocityParamToFloat(servoConfig()->ornithopter_ferocity_upstroke);\n        float fDeriv;\n        if (flappingSinusoid >= 0.1f) fDeriv = fDown;\n        else if (flappingSinusoid <= -0.1f) fDeriv = fUp;\n        else {\n            float tDeriv = (flappingSinusoid + 0.1f) * 5.0f;\n            fDeriv = fUp + (fDown - fUp) * tDeriv;\n        }\n        float tanhFd = tanhf(fDeriv);\n        float tanhArg = tanhf(fDeriv * flappingSinusoid);\n        float sech2 = 1.0f - tanhArg * tanhArg;\n        float shapedDerivative = fDeriv * flappingCosinusoid * sech2 / tanhFd;\n\n        flappingDerivative = shapedDerivative * thetadot;\n        normalizedFlappingIntegral = flappingDerivative / tcommand + 1.0f;\n        ornithopterFlapping = shapedFlappingSinusoid * flappingAmplitude;\n    }\n    else {\n        shapedFlappingSinusoid = 0.0f;\n        flappingDerivative = 0.0;\n        ornithopterFlapping = 0.0;\n        ondasAttenuation = 0.5;\n        ondasAttenuationDerivative = 1.0;\n        normalizedFlappingIntegral = 1.0;\n    }\n}\n>>>>>>> REPLACE\n", :path=>"src/main/flight/pid.c"}, :execution_time=>2.494}, {:content=>"Now update the ONDAS documentation with the unified formula:"}, {:id=>"call_00_mbwdTIjo0UoYlGbkjvpz4980", :name=>"read_file", :result=>{:content=>"\n## Oscillating Normalized Dynamic Adaptive Stabilization (ONDAS)\n\nOscillating Normalized Dynamic Adaptive Stabilization (ONDAS) is an innovative stabilization system specifically designed for flapping or oscillating systems. \nBy focusing on the central, most powerful part of the oscillating wave, ONDAS dynamically adapts to real-time data to maintain optimal stability and control while preventing the system from being destabilized by its own oscillations. This system leverages advanced normalization and dynamic adjustment techniques to minimize the impact of extreme errors, ensuring efficient and stable performance in varying conditions.\n\n\n### Key Features\n\n* **Oscillating Focus**: ONDAS emphasizes the stabilization of systems with inherent oscillating or flapping motions. It intelligently adjusts to the natural rhythm of the system, ensuring smooth and efficient operation.\n* **Normalized Error Management**: By normalizing error inputs through focus on the central part of the oscillation where the most thrust and control authority are generated, ONDAS reduces the influence of extreme deviations introduced by flapping wings.\n* **Dynamic Adaptation**: ONDAS adjusts control parameters in real-time to maintain stability and prevent overshooting, especially during the powerful central phases of the flapping motion.\n* **Centralized Control**: The system prioritizes the central phase of the oscillation, where the most thrust and control authority are generated. This focus helps in achieving precise stabilization and avoiding overshooting.\n\n\n### How It Works\n\n1. *Error Filtering*: ONDAS applies an alpha filter to the error term based on the oscillation phase, throttle input, and user-defined control variables. This filtering process reduces the influence of extreme errors and focuses on the most controllable and predictable part of the wave.\n2. *Adaptive PID Control*: The filtered error is used in the PID (Proportional-Integral-Derivative) control loop. The PID parameters are dynamically adjusted to adapt to changing conditions, ensuring responsive and stable control.\n3. *Seamless Integration*: ONDAS integrates with the flapping control loop, ensuring that stabilization efforts complement the natural motion of the system without interfering with its power and efficiency.\n\n### Benefits\n\n* Improved Stability: Prevents destabilization caused by the system’s own oscillations, ensuring smooth and efficient operation.\n* Optimized Control: Focuses on the central part of the oscillation to achieve precise stabilization and avoid overshooting.\n* Real-Time Adaptation: Continuously adapts to real-time conditions, providing robust stabilization even in rapidly changing environments.\n", :execution_time=>0.008}, :args=>{:path=>"ONDAS.md"}, :execution_time=>0.008}, {:content=>""}, {:id=>"call_00_Itaa0i7afQoB7k1Mshfr8493", :name=>"patch_file", :result=>{:ok=>true, :execution_time=>0.29}, :args=>{:diff=>"<<<<<<< SEARCH\n:start_line:1\n-------\n\n## Oscillating Normalized Dynamic Adaptive Stabilization (ONDAS)\n\nOscillating Normalized Dynamic Adaptive Stabilization (ONDAS) is an innovative stabilization system specifically designed for flapping or oscillating systems. \nBy focusing on the central, most powerful part of the oscillating wave, ONDAS dynamically adapts to real-time data to maintain optimal stability and control while preventing the system from being destabilized by its own oscillations. This system leverages advanced normalization and dynamic adjustment techniques to minimize the impact of extreme errors, ensuring efficient and stable performance in varying conditions.\n\n\n### Key Features\n\n* **Oscillating Focus**: ONDAS emphasizes the stabilization of systems with inherent oscillating or flapping motions. It intelligently adjusts to the natural rhythm of the system, ensuring smooth and efficient operation.\n* **Normalized Error Management**: By normalizing error inputs through focus on the central part of the oscillation where the most thrust and control authority are generated, ONDAS reduces the influence of extreme deviations introduced by flapping wings.\n* **Dynamic Adaptation**: ONDAS adjusts control parameters in real-time to maintain stability and prevent overshooting, especially during the powerful central phases of the flapping motion.\n* **Centralized Control**: The system prioritizes the central phase of the oscillation, where the most thrust and control authority are generated. This focus helps in achieving precise stabilization and avoiding overshooting.\n\n\n### How It Works\n\n1. *Error Filtering*: ONDAS applies an alpha filter to the error term based on the oscillation phase, throttle input, and user-defined control variables. This filtering process reduces the influence of extreme errors and focuses on the most controllable and predictable part of the wave.\n2. *Adaptive PID Control*: The filtered error is used in the PID (Proportional-Integral-Derivative) control loop. The PID parameters are dynamically adjusted to adapt to changing conditions, ensuring responsive and stable control.\n3. *Seamless Integration*: ONDAS integrates with the flapping control loop, ensuring that stabilization efforts complement the natural motion of the system without interfering with its power and efficiency.\n\n### Benefits\n\n* Improved Stability: Prevents destabilization caused by the system's own oscillations, ensuring smooth and efficient operation.\n* Optimized Control: Focuses on the central part of the oscillation to achieve precise stabilization and avoid overshooting.\n* Real-Time Adaptation: Continuously adapts to real-time conditions, providing robust stabilization even in rapidly changing environments.\n=======\n## ONDAS + Ferocity: Unified Flapping Stabilization\n\nOscillating Normalized Dynamic Adaptive Stabilization (ONDAS) is a phase-gated PID attenuation system that concentrates control authority at midstroke — the aerodynamic power phase — and suppresses it at stroke reversal. \n\n**Ferocity** is a wave-shaping parameter that distorts the sinusoidal wing trajectory toward a rectangular wave, allowing asymmetric control of downstroke vs upstroke aggressiveness. Together they form a unified stabilization architecture.\n\n### The Unified Formula\n\n```\nshapedWave(θ) = tanh(F · sinθ) / tanh(F)      where F ∈ [1.0, 8.0]\nondasAttenuation = −|shapedWave| + 0.5        range [−0.5, +0.5]\n```\n\n**Ferocity F** is independently tunable for downstroke (`ornithopter_ferocity_downstroke`) and upstroke (`ornithopter_ferocity_upstroke`), with a smooth blend zone at the zero crossing.\n\n| Ferocity | Wave Shape | ONDAS Effect |\n|----------|-----------|--------------|\n| 1.0 (default-ish) | Near-pure sine | Broad PID window, gentle gating |\n| 4.0 | Moderately squared | Narrower, sharper PID window |\n| 8.0 (max) | Near-rectangular | Very tight PID window at midstroke only |\n\nHigher ferocity → wing moves earlier and stays longer at full deflection → more thrust per stroke (less efficient) → ONDAS window naturally sharpens to match the compressed power phase.\n\n### Asymmetric Ferocity for Pitch Authority\n\n- **Higher downstroke ferocity** → more rectangular power stroke → stronger pitch-up impulse\n- **Higher upstroke ferocity** → more rectangular recovery stroke → stronger pitch-down impulse\n\nThis provides a secondary pitch trimming mechanism orthogonal to PID, exploiting the wing kinematics directly.\n\n### Key Features\n\n* **Phase-Gated PID**: PID authority modulated by `−|shapedWave| + 0.5` — amplified at midstroke, suppressed at stroke reversal\n* **Wave-Shaped Kinematics**: `tanh(F·sinθ)/tanh(F)` morphs from pure sine to near-square wave with a single parameter\n* **Asymmetric Stroke Control**: Independent ferocity for downstroke and upstroke enables aerodynamic pitch trimming\n* **Natural Resonance**: Ferocity sharpens the ONDAS window automatically — no separate tuning required for the attenuation profile\n* **Dynamic Adaptation**: Second-order ODE wing model drives phase; ferocity shapes the spatial waveform; ONDAS gates the PID\n\n### How It Works\n\n1. **Wing ODE** (`calculateFlappingFromThrottle`): `θ̈ = k₀·T_cmd − k₂·ω` — throttle drives frequency, phase θ evolves\n2. **Ferocity Shaping** (`applyFerocityWaveShaping`): `shapedWave = tanh(F·sinθ)/tanh(F)` — morphs sinusoid toward rectangle\n3. **ONDAS Gating**: `ondasAttenuation = −|shapedWave| + 0.5` — PID amplified at midstroke, suppressed at extremities\n4. **Servo Output**: `ornithopterFlapping = shapedWave · amplitude` — shaped wave drives servo positions\n\n### CLI Parameters\n\n| Parameter | Range | Default | Description |\n|-----------|-------|---------|-------------|\n| `ornithopter_ferocity_downstroke` | 1–100 | 12 | Ferocity on downstroke (1=sinusoidal, 100=rectangular) |\n| `ornithopter_ferocity_upstroke` | 1–100 | 12 | Ferocity on upstroke |\n| `ondas_gain` | -100–100 | 10 | ONDAS attenuation gain (0=off) |\n| `ondas_gain2` | -100–100 | 10 | I-term scaling factor |\n| `ondas_gain3` | -100–100 | 10 | D-term modulation |\n\n### Benefits\n\n* **Improved Stability**: Phase-gated PID prevents fighting the wing's own oscillation\n* **Asymmetric Thrust Control**: Per-stroke ferocity enables aerodynamic pitch authority without PID\n* **Automatic Window Sharpening**: ONDAS gain window narrows naturally as ferocity increases\n* **Single-Parameter Wave Morphing**: From sinusoidal to rectangular with one number per stroke\n>>>>>>> REPLACE\n", :path=>"ONDAS.md"}, :execution_time=>0.291}, {:content=>"Let me verify there are no other files that need to know about the new globals, and then try a build:"}, {:id=>"call_00_Rv6Ojrr7y67CsF90VbLk1040", :name=>"run_command", :result=>{:ok=>true, :exit_status=>0, :result=>"Command output: src/main/flight/pid.h:207:extern float ornithopterFlapping;\n\n(exit 0)", :execution_time=>0.635}, :args=>{:cmd=>"grep -rn 'extern.*flappingSinusoid\\|extern.*shapedFlapping\\|extern.*ornithopterFlapping' src/main/ | head -10"}, :execution_time=>0.635}