entry {:prompt=>"wait", :answer=>"*tending to the scrying pool, steadying the waters...*\n\nOf course — I spoke too much, and too quickly. I'll listen.", :tool_call_count=>0, :execution_time=>3.947303, :timestamp=>nil, :tool_calls_json=>"[]", :created_at=>"2026-07-14 01:31:02"}
entry {:prompt=>"\nthese are good points... i tried to introduce a better mapping of PID to aerolastic effects but just introduced new instabilities ... i think my tendencies have been working but are not fully developed. i have been working on a new flapping parameter called ferocity in another project for rp2040. ferocity is an extra parameter that may apply on downstroke or upstroke, this part of the wave is mathematically transformed into a more and more near rectangular wave, which is starting to move earlier and stays more at higher speed. generally more ferocity is more thrust, but a bit in efficient. ferocity on downstroke adds therefore more pitch up and ferocity on upstroke adds more elevator down effect from the pulse. this kind of wave shaping that is regarding up and downstroke separately is key for efficient stabilization and you can see in my code i have already been doing that. please check my new improvement of the flapping algorithm and introduce them in this project and further think about how we can combine and enhance the stabilization techniques and find a new formula. you may create a task for this\n\nrepo: /Users/d/Desktop/HOI_KOSMOI/paraeksperiment/Arduino/libraries/o-grande-codigo-da-gralha-azul\n", :answer=>"---\n\n*The glyphs settle into their final alignment...*\n\n## What Was Wrought\n\nThe ferocity wave-shaping from **Gralha Azul** has been woven into OrniFlight's heart. Here's the summary:\n\n### Files Modified\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| <file path=\"src/main/flight/servos.h\" line=\"137\">servos.h:137-138</file> | Added `ornithopter_ferocity_downstroke` and `ornithopter_ferocity_upstroke` to `servoConfig_t` |\n| <file path=\"src/main/flight/servos.c\" line=\"77\">servos.c:77-78</file> | PG defaults: both ferocity params = 12 (~1.78, mild near-sine) |\n| <file path=\"src/main/cli/settings.c\" line=\"1434\">settings.c:1434-1435</file> | CLI entries: range 1–100 |\n| <file path=\"src/main/flight/pid.c\" line=\"583\">pid.c:583-665</file> | Core: `applyFerocityWaveShaping()`, unified ONDAS+ferocity in `calculateFlappingFromThrottle()` |\n| <file>ONDAS.md</file> | Full documentation rewrite with unified formula |\n\n### The Unified Formula\n\n```\nshapedWave(θ) = tanh(F · sinθ) / tanh(F)      F ∈ [1.0, 8.0]\nondasAttenuation = −|shapedWave| + 0.5\n```\n\nThe elegance: **higher ferocity automatically sharpens the ONDAS window**. No separate tuning needed — as the wave becomes more rectangular, the PID authority window narrows to match the compressed power stroke. The ONDAS gating rides the ferocity-shaped wave natively.\n\n### CLI Parameters\n\n```\nornithopter_ferocity_downstroke = 12    (1-100, maps to ferocity 1.0-8.0)\nornithopter_ferocity_upstroke   = 12\n```\n\n### Your Intuition Was Right\n\nThe asymmetric ferocity (different values for downstroke vs upstroke) creates an aerodynamic pitch authority that's orthogonal to PID, exploiting wing kinematics directly — exactly as you described with \"ferocity on downstroke adds pitch up.\" The ONDAS attenuation window reshapes itself around whatever waveform the ferocity produces, so the stabilization stays phase-locked to the actual wing motion, not a pure sine.\n\nWould you like me to explore any particular aspect — perhaps the phase-shift interaction with ferocity, or a simulation harness to test the resonance behavior?", :tool_call_count=>82, :execution_time=>408.894843, :timestamp=>nil, :tool_calls_json=>"[{\"content\":\"*The scrying pool shifts to a new star — the Gralha Azul repository...*\\n\\nLet me first survey the new project to understand the ferocity wave-shaping, then we'll weave it into OrniFlight.\",\"args\":null,\"result\":null},{\"id\":\"call_00_HVnzS3XL5YUgQUB5Phgn3142\",\"name\":\"aegis\",\"result\":{\"aegis_notes\":[{\"id\":2,\"content\":\"ONDAS implementation in pid.c: State variables flappingSinusoid, flappingSinusoid2, flappingCosinusoid, flappingAmplitude, ornithopterFlapping, ondasAttenuation, ondasAttenuationDerivative, flappingDerivative, normalizedFlappingIntegral.\\n\\ncalculateFlappingFromThrottle(): Uses second-order ODE (omega, theta) driven by throttle to model flapping dynamics. Computes ondasAttenuation = -fabs(flappingSinusoid)+0.5 (center-weighted). ondasAttenuationDerivative = cos²θ-sin²θ. Below GLIDE_MODE_THRESHOLD:...\",\"tags\":\"code,ondas,flapping,pid\",\"links\":\"src/main/flight/pid.c,src/main/flight/pid.h\",\"created_at\":\"2026-07-14 01:17:15\",\"score\":7},{\"id\":4,\"content\":\"ONDAS full architecture: Second-order ODE solver (calculateFlappingFromThrottle) at pid.c:585-619 drives flapping kinematics: θ̈ = k₀·T_cmd − k₂·ω with k₀=1.0, k₂=10.0. Outputs: flappingSinusoid, flappingCosinusoid, flappingDerivative, ondasAttenuation (= -|sinθ| + 0.5), ondasAttenuationDerivative (= cos²θ − sin²θ), normalizedFlappingIntegral (= flappingDerivative/tcommand + 1.0), ornithopterFlapping. Glide mode below GLIDE_MODE_THRESHOLD (1040): wings lock at ornithopter_glide_deg * 5 servo uni...\",\"tags\":\"code,ondas,flapping,pid,architecture\",\"links\":\"src/main/flight/pid.c,src/main/flight/servos.c,src/main/flight/servos.h,src/main/cli/settings.c,src/main/fc/controlrate_profile.c\",\"created_at\":\"2026-07-14 01:19:55\",\"score\":7},{\"id\":1,\"content\":\"OrniFlight: open-source flight control for servo-flapping ornithopters, forked from Betaflight 4.0.6. FORKNAME=orniflight. GPL v3 licensed. Key innovation: ONDAS (Oscillating Normalized Dynamic Adaptive Stabilization) for flapping-wing flight dynamics.\\n\\nProject structure: src/main/ with standard Betaflight layout — flight/, fc/, drivers/, sensors/, io/, cli/, msp/, rx/, osd/, telemetry/, pg/, config/. Build via Makefile targeting STM32F3/F4/F7 MCUs.\",\"tags\":\"code,structure,overview\",\"links\":\"README.md,Makefile,src/main/flight/\",\"created_at\":\"2026-07-14 01:17:15\",\"score\":4}],\"aegis_orientation\":{\"tags\":[\"task\",\"ferocity\",\"ondas\",\"porting\"],\"summary\":\"User wants to port \\\"ferocity\\\" wave-shaping from RP2040 project (o-grande-codigo-da-gralha-azul) into OrniFlight, combining with ONDAS stabilization...\",\"temperature\":0.0,\"working_dir\":null,\"thinking\":null},\"execution_time\":0.006},\"args\":{\"summary\":\"User wants to port \\\"ferocity\\\" wave-shaping from RP2040 project (o-grande-codigo-da-gralha-azul) into OrniFlight, combining with ONDAS stabilization. Need to study the new algorithm first.\",\"tags\":[\"task\",\"ferocity\",\"ondas\",\"porting\"],\"temperature\":0.0},\"execution_time\":0.008},{\"content\":\"\",\"args\":null,\"result\":null},{\"id\":\"call_00_vAK3Ny2ShVF3w1vnFw6d7732\",\"name\":\"run_command\",\"result\":{\"ok\":true,\"exit_status\":0,\"result\":\"Command output: /Users/d/Desktop/HOI_KOSMOI/paraeksperiment/Arduino/libraries/o-grande-codigo-da-gralha-azul/CHANGELOG.md\\n/Users/d/Desktop/HOI_KOSMOI/paraeksperiment/Arduino/libraries/o-grande-codigo-da-gralha-azul/o-grande-codigo-da-gralha-azul.ino\\n/Users/d/Desktop/HOI_KOSMOI/paraeksperiment/Ard...\",\"execution_time\":0.112},\"args\":{\"cmd\":\"find /Users/d/Desktop/HOI_KOSMOI/paraeksperiment/Arduino/libraries/o-grande-codigo-da-gralha-azul -type f | head -80\"},\"execution_time\":0.112},{\"content\":\"\",\"args\":null,\"result\":null},{\"id\":\"call_00_wpslslU7x7JgRp1oBIWW1115\",\"name\":\"run_command\",\"result\":{\"ok\":true,\"exit_status\":0,\"result\":\"Command output: /Users/d/Desktop/HOI_KOSMOI/paraeksperiment/Arduino/libraries/o-grande-codigo-da-gralha-azul/.gitignore\\n/Users/d/Desktop/HOI_KOSMOI/paraeksperiment/Arduino/libraries/o-grande-codigo-da-gralha-azul/CHANGELOG.md\\n/Users/d/Desktop/HOI_KOSMOI/paraeksperiment/Arduino/libraries/o-grande-...\",\"execution_time\":0.108},\"args\":{\"cmd\":\"find /Users/d/Desktop/HOI_KOSMOI/paraeksperiment/Arduino/libraries/o-grande-codigo-da-gralha-azul -type f -not -path '*/.git/*' | sort\"},\"execution_time\":0.109},{\"content\":\"Now let me read the key source files — documentation first, then the flapping algori