truncate_tool_calls_by_priority=[{:content=>""}, {:id=>"call_00_uwu33BBUlki2MG1Xg60h4431", :name=>"task_get_previous_results", :result=>{:ok=>true, :task_id=>2, :results=>{"1"=>"<p><strong>Nigredo Complete — Prima Materia Understood</strong></p>\n\n<h2>OrniFlight System Identity</h2>\n\n<p>OrniFlight is a <strong>flapping-wing flight controller</strong> forked from Betaflight 4.0.6, targeting STM32F3/F4/F7 MCUs. Its core innovation is <strong>ONDAS</strong> (Oscillating Normalized Dynamic Adaptive Stabilization) — a three-layer control system where PID terms modulate wing-trajectory parameters rather than servo offset.</p>\n\n<h2>Core Files Mapped</h2>\n\n<h3>Flight Core (read complete):</h3>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>pid.c</strong> (~1000 lines): Wing ODE (<code>θ̈ = k₀·T_cmd − k₂·ω</code>), three-channel breathing-pause modulation (P→phase advance/k0, D→ferocity, I→asymmetry), ferocity wave shaping (<code>tanh(F·sinθ)/tanh(F)</code>), SSFF stroke-synchronous feed-forward, aeroelastic PID gain adjustment, glide mode (throttle &lt; 1040)</li>\n<li><strong>pid.h</strong>: PID struct, pidProfile_t with all Betaflight PID parameters, PG registrations</li>\n<li><strong>mixer.c</strong>: Motor mixer with MIXER_SERVO_ORNITHOPTER (27), mixerOrnithopter[] 4-motor table, throttle handling, airmode, crash flip</li>\n<li><strong>mixer.h</strong>: mixerMode_e enum, motorMixer_t, mixerConfig_t</li>\n<li><strong>servos.c</strong>: servoMixerOrni[] rules, applyFlappingToServos() — flapping signal = <code>ornithopterFlapping/100 * (motor[i] - 1000)</code>, glide at throttle &lt; 1040, servo lowpass, writeServos()</li>\n<li><strong>servos.h</strong>: servoConfig_t with all 14 orni-specific fields, INPUT_STABILIZED_FLAPPING_0..3, SERVO_ORNITHOPTER_1..4</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Configuration &amp; Build:</h3>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>settings.c</strong>: CLI valueTable with all orni parameters exposed at PG_SERVO_CONFIG</li>\n<li><strong>common_pre.h</strong>: USE_ORNI_MIXER_ONLY for FLASH&gt;256, undefs 8 propeller features (DSHOT, RPM_FILTER, LAUNCH_CONTROL, etc.)</li>\n<li><strong>common_post.h</strong>: Cascade dependency cleanup</li>\n<li><strong>Makefile</strong>: Standard Betaflight build, FORKNAME=orniflight, LTO + -Ofast</li>\n<li><strong>pg.h</strong>: GLIDE_MODE_THRESHOLD = 1040</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Control Rate:</h3>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>controlrate_profile.h</strong>: flap_speed_modificator (uint16, frequency trim), phase_shift_scale (int8, legacy)</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Simulation &amp; Docs:</h3>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>sim_ferocity.rb</strong>: 6-mode Ruby simulation matching firmware physics</li>\n<li><strong>ONDAS.md</strong>: Three-layer theory documentation</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>Parameter Space</h2>\n\n<p>14 orni-specific parameters in servoConfig_t: flap_base_frequency (12), flap_base_amplitude (60), ornithopter_glide_deg (-30), ondas_gain/gain2/gain3 (20/20/10), aeroelastic_glide/flap_coefficient (40/40), ferocity_downstroke/upstroke (12/12), ssff_gain (0). Plus flap_speed_modificator and phase_shift_scale in controlRateConfig_t.</p>\n\n<h2>Architecture Data Flow</h2>\n<pre><code>RC Throttle → calculateFlappingFromThrottle() → Wing ODE (θ,ω)\n  → Ferocity Wave Shaping → shapedFlappingSinusoid\n  → ornithopterFlapping = shaped * amplitude\n\nGyro → PID Loop → P/I/D per axis\n  → PITCH: SSFF + Three-Channel Modulation + Aeroelastic Gain Adjustment\n  → pidData[axis].Sum → mixer table → motor[i]\n\nServo Mixer: INPUT_STABILIZED_FLAPPING_i = ornithopterFlapping/100 * (motor[i]-1000)\n  → combined with roll/pitch/yaw stabilization → servo PWM\n</code></pre>\n<h2>Anti-Gravity Status</h2>\n\n<p>Completely neutered under USE_ORNI_MIXER_ONLY — function signatures kept for callers, internals no-op.</p>\n\n<h2>Key Numbers</h2>\n\n<ul>\n<li>Wing ODE: k₀=1.0, k₂=10.0 (hardcoded)</li>\n<li>Ferocity range: [1.0, 8.0], mapped from CLI [1,100]</li>\n<li>Phase modulation range: [0.5, 2.0]</li>\n<li>Ferocity modulation range: [-0.5, 0.5]</li>\n<li>Asymmetry bias range: [-3.0, 3.0]</li>\n<li>Glide threshold: 1040 (PWM)</li>\n<li>Flash usage: 99.43% on F7 target</li>\n<li>PID loop on PITCH axis only drives ONDAS modulation</li>\n</ul>\n", "2"=>"<h2>Albedo: Purified Solution Definition</h2>\n\n<h3>Document Architecture</h3>\n\n<p>Seven documents + index, each with a single organizing principle:</p>\n\n<table><thead>\n<tr>\n<th>#</th>\n<th>Document</th>\n<th>Organizing Question</th>\n<th>~Length</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>00</td>\n<td>INDEX.md</td>\n<td>How should this be read?</td>\n<td>1 page</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>01</td>\n<td>ARCHITECTURE.md</td>\n<td>How does the system fit together?</td>\n<td>8-12pp</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>02</td>\n<td>CONTROL_THEORY.md</td>\n<td>What are the governing mathematics?</td>\n<td>10-15pp</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>03</td>\n<td>PARAMETER_SPACE.md</td>\n<td>What can be tuned and how?</td>\n<td>8-12pp</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>04</td>\n<td>IDENTITY.md</td>\n<td>What IS OrniFlight?</td>\n<td>4-6pp</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>05</td>\n<td>CRITIQUE.md</td>\n<td>Where does it break?</td>\n<td>8-12pp</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>06</td>\n<td>IMPROVEMENT_VISION.md</td>\n<td>Where should it go?</td>\n<td>6-10pp</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>07</td>\n<td>SIMULATION.md</td>\n<td>How do we validate without hardware?</td>\n<td>6-8pp</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\n<h3>Document Interfaces (Cross-Reference Schema)</h3>\n<pre><code>00_INDEX ──reads──▶ all documents (TOC + reading paths)\n\n01_ARCHITECTURE ──explains──▶ 02_CONTROL_THEORY (data flow → math)\n                ──locates────▶ 03_PARAMETER_SPACE (components → params)\n                ──informs────▶ 04_IDENTITY (structure → identity)\n\n02_CONTROL_THEORY ──parameterizes──▶ 03_PARAMETER_SPACE (math → tunables)\n                  ──validates───────▶ 07_SIMULATION (theory → verification)\n\n03_PARAMETER_SPACE ──gaps──▶ 05_CRITIQUE (missing MSP → weakness)\n                   ──feeds──▶ 06_IMPROVEMENT_VISION (params → autotune)\n\n04_IDENTITY ──contrasts──▶ 05_CRITIQUE (ideal vs reality)\n            ──guides──────▶ 06_IMPROVEMENT_VISION (principles → roadmap)\n\n05_CRITIQUE ──motivates──▶ 06_IMPROVEMENT_VISION (problems → solutions)\n\n07_SIMULATION ──references──▶ 02_CONTROL_THEORY (matching physics)\n              ──tunes────────▶ 03_PARAMETER_SPACE (sweep → defaults)\n</code></pre>\n<p><strong>Cross-reference syntax</strong>: <code>See [02_CONTROL_THEORY.md#wing-ode](&quot;the Wing ODE&quot;)</code> — internal references use the document slug, external use <code>&lt;file&gt;</code> tags.</p>\n\n<h3>Source-to-Document Mapping</h3>\n\n<table><thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Source File</th>\n<th>Primary Document</th>\n<th>Secondary</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>pid.c (1857L)</td>\n<td>02 (ODE, 3ch, ferocity), 01 (PID flow)</td>\n<td>05 (magic numbers, dead code)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>pid.h</td>\n<td>03 (pidProfile_t fields)</td>\n<td>01 (struct relations)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>servos.c (662L)</td>\n<td>01 (servo mixer path), 02 (glide state)</td>\n<td>05 (naming inconsistencies)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>servos.h</td>\n<td>03 (servoConfig_t, all 14 orni fields)</td>\n<td>—</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>mixer.c (1078L)</td>\n<td>01 (throttle→motor path)</td>\n<td>05 (deadband complexity)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>mixer.h</td>\n<td>01 (mixerMode_e)</td>\n<td>—</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>settings.c (1442L)</td>\n<td>03 (CLI exposure table)</td>\n<td>05 (MSP gaps)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>common_pre.h</td>\n<td>01 (feature defines), 04 (identity)</td>\n<td>05 (8 dead features)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>common_post.h</td>\n<td>01 (feature cascade)</td>\n<td>—</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>controlrate_profile.h</td>\n<td>03 (flap_speed_modificator)</td>\n<td>05 (legacy phase_shift_scale)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>pg.h</td>\n<td>03 (GLIDE_MODE_THRESHOLD)</td>\n<td>—</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>msp.c, msp_protocol.h</td>\n<td>03 (MSP commands), 05 (exposure gaps)</td>\n<td>06 (MSP expansion)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>sim_ferocity.rb (582L)</td>\n<td>07 (full analysis)</td>\n<td>02 (validation)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>ONDAS.md (79L)</td>\n<td>02, 04 (source theory)</td>\n<td>—</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Makefile</td>\n<td>04 (build identity)</td>\n<td>05 (flash budget)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\n<h3>Document Templates</h3>\n\n<h4>01_ARCHITECTURE.md</h4>\n<pre><code># Architecture\n\n## System Overview (Mermaid component graph)\n## Initialization Sequence (main.c → init → scheduler)\n## PID Loop Flow (pidController() step-by-step)\n## Data Flow Diagram (Gyro→PID→Mixer→Servos Mermaid)\n## Three-Channel Modulation Pathway\n## Glide Mode State Machine (Mermaid state diagram)\n## ONDAS Wing-Phase Feedback Loop\n## Feature Define Cascade (common_pre.h → common_post.h)\n## Memory Layout (PG registrations, struct sizes)\n</code></pre>\n<h4>02_CONTROL_THEORY.md</h4>\n<pre><code># Control Theory\n\n## The Wing ODE: θ̈ = k₀·T_cmd − k₂·ω\n  - Derivation, discretization, parameter sensitivity\n## Ferocity Wave Shaping: tanh(F·sinθ)/tanh(F)\n  - Mathematical justification, normalization proof, edge cases\n## Three-Channel Breathing-Pause Modulation\n  - P→k₀ phase advance: mechanics, range analysis\n  - D→ferocity modulation: breathing pause depth\n  - I→asymmetry bias: up/down thrust balance\n## Stroke-Synchronous Feed-Forward (SSFF)\n  - Half-stroke error accumulation, zero-crossing detection\n## Aeroelastic Gain Adjustment\n  - Glide vs flap coefficient blending\n## Phase Lock: θ as PID timing reference\n## Complete Transfer Function (symbolic)\n## Numerical Analysis (stability, oscillation modes)\n</code></pre>\n<h4>03_PARAMETER_SPACE.md</h4>\n<pre><code># Parameter Space\n\n## servoConfig_t (14 orni fields)\n  - Table: Name | CLI | Type | Range | Default | MSP? | Description | Interactions\n## controlRateConfig_t (2 orni fields)\n## pidProfile_t (orni-relevant subset)\n## mixerConfig_t (orni-relevant subset)\n## Hardcoded Constants (k₀, k₂, GLIDE_MODE_THRESHOLD, blend zones)\n## Parameter Interaction Matrix\n  - ferocity_down × ferocity_up × ondas_gain\n  - aeroelastic_glide × aeroelastic_flap × throttle curve\n## MSP Exposure Gaps (ondas_gain2/gain3, ssff_gain, aeroelastic_*)\n## CLI vs MSP vs PG mapping table\n</code></pre>\n<h4>04_IDENTITY.md</h4>\n<pre><code># Project Identity\n\n## What OrniFlight IS\n  - Flapping-wing FC derived from Betaflight 4.0.6\n  - Core innovation: trajectory modulation, not moment modulation\n  - GPLv3, open-source, research-community oriented\n## Design Philosophy\n  - PID modulates wing trajectory parameters\n  - Physics-driven (ODE) not empirical\n  - Servo as primary actuator, not ESC\n## Target Hardware &amp; Constraints\n  - STM32F3/F4/F7, PWM servos\n  - 99.43% flash on F7 — hard ceiling\n## Community &amp; Ecosystem\n  - Configurator integration status\n  - Relationship to Betaflight upstream\n## Design Principles (numbered, each with rationale)\n</code></pre>\n<h4>05_CRITIQUE.md</h4>\n<pre><code># Critique\n\n## Strengths (each with evidence)\n  - Elegant tanh wave-shaping mathematics\n  - Novel three-channel control paradigm\n  - Clean separation of flapping physics from stabilization\n  - Working simulation harness matching firmware physics\n  - SSFF working in parallel with ONDAS\n\n## Weaknesses (each with file:line evidence)\n  - Dead Code Inventory (8 propeller features #undef&#39;d, anti-gravity stubs)\n  - MSP Exposure Gaps (ondas_gain2/gain3, ssff_gain, aeroelastic_*)\n  - Tight Flash Budget (99.43% — no headroom for features)\n  - Hardcoded Magic Numbers (k₀=1.0, k₂=10.0, blend zones, thresholds)\n  - Naming Inconsistencies (flapping vs ornithopter vs flap, gain/gain2/gain3)\n  - Missing Guardrails (parameter interactions unvalidated)\n  - Untested Edge Cases (zero throttle, failsafe, sensor loss)\n  - Single-Axis ONDAS (PITCH only, no ROLL differential ferocity)\n  - Legacy Artifacts (phase_shift_scale in controlrate_profile.h)\n  - Comment Quality (sparse in critical sections)\n\n## Code Quality Assessment\n  - Cohesion: pid.c owns too much (ODE + PID + ONDAS + SSFF + aeroelastic)\n  - Coupling: pid.c includes servos.h for ferocity params\n  - Error Handling: asserts present but no graceful degradation\n  - Testability: sim_ferocity.rb covers theory but not integration\n  - Duplication: ferocity clamping appears in 3 locations\n</code></pre>\n<h4>06_IMPROVEMENT_VISION.md</h4>\n<pre><code># Improvement Vision\n\n## Immediate (Next Release)\n  - MSP exposure for ondas_gain2, ondas_gain3, ssff_gain\n  - Remove legacy phase_shift_scale\n  - Unify parameter naming (proposal table)\n  - Flash budget: identify 2% reclaimable\n\n## Short-Term (1-3 Releases)\n  - Autotune: sim_ferocity.rb integration for PID/gain discovery\n  - CLI inter-parameter validation\n  - Blackbox logging for orni-specific signals (θ, ω, ferocity, modulation)\n  - Configurator three-channel UI\n  - Improved failsafe (glide-to-land descent profile)\n\n## Medium-Term (Architecture)\n  - Extract orni_flight.c from pid.c\n  - Pluggable airframe models (abstract wing physics)\n  - Multi-axis ONDAS (roll via differential ferocity)\n  - Adaptive ferocity from airspeed estimation\n  - DSP-based wing phase detection (no hall sensor)\n\n## Long-Term (Vision)\n  - Autonomous perch/land in glide mode\n  - Flocking/swarm via telemetry mesh\n  - Real-time efficiency optimization\n  - Species-specific wing profiles as config presets\n  - Actuator abstraction layer (servo, BLDC, SMA)\n</code></pre>\n<h4>07_SIMULATION.md</h4>\n<pre><code># Simulation\n\n## sim_ferocity.rb Overview (6 modes, 582 lines)\n## Mode: wave — Static wave shape analysis\n## Mode: flight — Full wing ODE + airframe + PID\n## Mode: sweep — 11×11 ferocity grid search\n## Mode: compare — Fixed vs SSFF side-by-side\n## Mode: derive — Velocity amplification by ferocity\n## Mode: prize — Full theory demonstration\n## Airframe Model (1st-order pitch dynamics, I_YY, PITCH_DAMP)\n## Key Findings from Sweeps\n## Tuning Methodology (sim-first, then hardware)\n## Limitations (no servo dynamics, no sensor noise, 2D only)\n</code></pre>\n<h3>Formatting Conventions</h3>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>File references</strong>: <code>&lt;file&gt;path:line&lt;/file&gt;</code> for code locations</li>\n<li><strong>Code</strong>: Fenced with <code>c (or</code>ruby for sim)</li>\n<li><strong>Math</strong>: LaTeX in <code>$...$</code> for inline, <code>$$...$$</code> for display</li>\n<li><strong>Diagrams</strong>: Mermaid <code>mermaid ...</code></li>\n<li><strong>Parameter tables</strong>: Markdown tables with columns: Name | CLI | Type | Range | Default | MSP | Description</li>\n<li><strong>Cross-references</strong>: <code>[DOCUMENT.md#anchor](descriptive text)</code> — internal; <code>&lt;file&gt;</code> — code</li>\n<li><strong>Tone</strong>: Technical but hermetic. Precise, no filler. Each section earns its length.</li>\n<li><strong>Heading depth</strong>: Max 3 levels (h2, h3, h4). No h1 except document title.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Completion Criteria (per document)</h3>\n\n<table><thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Document</th>\n<th>Done When</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>00</td>\n<td>All 7 docs listed with abstracts and 3 reading paths (user/dev/researcher)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>01</td>\n<td>3 Mermaid diagrams, full data flow traced gyro→servo, init sequence documented</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>02</td>\n<td>Every equation derived, every constant justified, sensitivity analysis included</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>03</td>\n<td>All 16+ orni params in tables, MSP gaps enumerated, interaction matrix filled</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>04</td>\n<td>Identity statement &lt;200 words, 5+ design principles, hardware constraints explicit</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>05</td>\n<td>Every weakness has file:line evidence, dead code catalogued, quality metrics given</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>06</td>\n<td>Every time horizon has 3+ concrete items, each with rationale and difficulty estimate</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>07</td>\n<td>All 6 modes documented, key sweep findings graphed, tuning methodology step-by-step</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\n<h3>Reading Paths (for INDEX.md)</h3>\n\n<ol>\n<li><strong>User Path</strong>: 04 → 03 → 02 (selected sections) → 01 (diagrams only)</li>\n<li><strong>Developer Path</strong>: 01 → 02 → 03 → 05 → 07</li>\n<li><strong>Researcher Path</strong>: 02 → 07 → 03 → 06 → 05</li>\n</ol>\n", "3"=>"<h2>Citrinitas: Golden Implementation Paths</h2>\n\n<h3>Source Survey — Key Discoveries Shaping Path Selection</h3>\n\n<table>\n<tr><th>Finding</th><th>Impact</th></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>Simulation-Firmware Gap</strong>: <code>sim_ferocity.rb</code> uses old single-channel ONDAS gate (<code>ondas_attn = -|shaped| + 0.5</code>), firmware uses three-channel (P→k0, D→ferocity, I→asymmetry). Simulation predates the breathing-pause architecture.</td><td>Document 07 (SIMULATION) must explicitly map old→new and show the delta. Document 02 (CONTROL_THEORY) must present both for comparison.</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>ONDAS.md Outdated</strong>: References only <code>ondas_gain</code> and <code>ondas_gain2</code> (mislabeled \"I-term scaling\"). No mention of the three-channel system, D-term ferocity modulation, or I-term asymmetry bias.</td><td>Document 02 supersedes ONDAS.md. Document 04 (IDENTITY) can reference ONDAS.md as the philosophical seed.</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>MSP Exposure Gap</strong>: Only <code>ornithopter_glide_deg</code> and <code>ondas_gain</code> exposed via MSP (and <code>ondas_gain</code> is UINT8 in MSP, INT8 in CLI — range mismatch). 7 orni params are CLI-only.</td><td>Document 03 (PARAMETER_SPACE) must enumerate every MSP gap. Document 06 (IMPROVEMENT) must price each gap.</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>pid.h Dead Declarations</strong>: Commented-out <code>flappingSinusoid</code>, <code>flappingCosinusoid</code>, <code>coFlapping</code>, <code>flappingAmplitude</code>, <code>flappingSquared</code>, <code>flappingDerivative</code> — 6 dead externs.</td><td>Document 05 (CRITIQUE) dead code inventory.</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>sim_ferocity.rb Bug</strong>: Duplicate \"Velocity Amplification by Ferocity\" code block in <code>mode_prize</code> (lines 403-434 and 438-469).</td><td>Document 07 must note this. Document 05 as code quality item.</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>Hardcoded Magic Numbers</strong>: k₀=1.0, k₂=10.0, three scale factors (0.00005, 0.0003, 0.0001), blend zone ±0.1 rad, GLIDE_MODE_THRESHOLD=1040, amplitude scalars.</td><td>Document 02 must derive/justify each. Document 05 as weakness.</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>servos.h Clean</strong>: All 14 orni fields well-named, properly typed. Enum complete.</td><td>Document 03 has a solid foundation. Document 05 can praise this.</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<h3>Per-Document Path Selection</h3>\n\n<h4>00_INDEX.md — \"How should this be read?\"</h4>\n\n<p><strong>Golden Path: Three-Reader Architecture</strong>. Three curated reading paths (User/Developer/Researcher) with per-section time estimates and dependency arrows. Each path lists documents in order with \"skip to section X if you only need Y.\" A quick-reference table maps common questions (\"How do I tune ferocity?\", \"What's the wing ODE?\", \"Where's the dead code?\") to document:section. <em>~1 page. Straightforward — no alternative paths needed.</em></p>\n\n<h4>01_ARCHITECTURE.md — \"How does the system fit together?\"</h4>\n\n<p><strong>Golden Path: Mermaid + Embedded Code Snippets (Hybrid B/C)</strong>. Three Mermaid diagrams: (1) Component Graph — sensors→IMU→PID→mixer→servos with data types on edges; (2) Data Flow Sequence — gyro sample→filter cascade→PID computation→three-channel modulation→calculateFlappingFromThrottle→servo PWM, with timing annotations; (3) Feature Define Cascade — common_pre.h→common_post.h decision tree. Each diagram followed by a ~2-sentence commentary grounding it in code (<code>&lt;file&gt;pid.c:NNN&lt;/file&gt;</code>). Init sequence from main.c documented as bullet timeline. Rejected: pure ASCII (no interactivity), pure Mermaid (no code grounding). <em>~8-10 pages.</em></p>\n\n<h4>02_CONTROL_THEORY.md — \"What are the governing mathematics?\"</h4>\n\n<p><strong>Golden Path: Engineering-Annotated Math with Simulation Validation (Hybrid B/C)</strong>. Each equation block: (a) LaTeX derivation, (b) physical interpretation in 1-2 sentences, (c) parameter sensitivity from sim sweep data, (d) firmware location cross-reference. Wing ODE → Ferocity Wave Shaping → Three-Channel Modulation → SSFF → Aeroelastic Gain → Complete Transfer Function. Critical: document both the <em>current</em> three-channel system AND the <em>simulated</em> single-channel gate model, with a migration comparison section. Rejected: pure academic (loses the code), pure code-annotated (loses mathematical rigor). The sim sweep data (11×11 grid from <code>mode sweep</code>) provides empirical sensitivity curves for ferocity combinations. <em>~10-14 pages.</em></p>\n\n<h4>03_PARAMETER_SPACE.md — \"What can be tuned and how?\"</h4>\n\n<p><strong>Golden Path: Grouped Tables + Interaction Matrix + MSP Gap Analysis (Path B)</strong>. Four parameter groups: (1) Flapping Physics (frequency, amplitude, glide), (2) Ferocity (down/up stroke shaping), (3) ONDAS Three-Channel (gain/gain2/gain3), (4) Aeroelastic (glide/flap coefficients, SSFF). Each group: table with Name|CLI|Type|Range|Default|MSP?|Description|Interactions. Followed by Interaction Matrix — a heat-map-style table showing which parameter pairs have compound effects (e.g., <code>ondas_gain × ferocity_downstroke</code>). MSP gap enumeration with proposed MSP command IDs. Hardcoded constants section with their locations. Rejected: flat table (loses grouping logic), interactive scenarios (too verbose). <em>~8-12 pages.</em></p>\n\n<h4>04_IDENTITY.md — \"What IS OrniFlight?\"</h4>\n\n<p><strong>Golden Path: Self-Definition + Contrast Trace (Path A+B)</strong>. Identity statement (&lt;200 words): \"OrniFlight is a flapping-wing flight controller...\". Five design principles each with rationale and code evidence: (1) Trajectory Modulation Not Moment Modulation, (2) Physics-Driven Not Empirical, (3) Servo-Centric Not ESC-Centric, (4) Open-Source Research Platform, (5) Hermetic Not Fragmented. One contrast section: \"How OrniFlight Differs from Betaflight\" — not a comparison, but a clarification of divergence points (8 #undef'd features, anti-gravity neutered, servo mixer vs motor mixer). Hardware constraints (STM32F3/F4/F7, 99.43% flash on F7). Community orientation. Rejected: pure narrative (loses precision), pure comparative (defines by negation). <em>~4-6 pages.</em></p>\n\n<h4>05_CRITIQUE.md — \"Where does it break?\"</h4>\n\n<p><strong>Golden Path: Strengths-First, Then Categorized Weaknesses with Evidence (Path C)</strong>. Six strengths with file:line evidence establishing credibility. Weaknesses organized by category: (A) Code Quality — duplication, naming inconsistencies, magic numbers, dead code catalog (8 #undef'd features, 6 commented-out externs, anti-gravity stubs); (B) Architecture — pid.c owns too much (ODE+PID+ONDAS+SSFF+aeroelastic in one file), PITCH-only ONDAS, no graceful degradation; (C) Gaps — MSP exposure for 7 params, simulation-firmware mismatch, ONDAS.md outdated; (D) Risk — 99.43% flash, untested edge cases (zero throttle, failsafe, sensor loss). Each weakness: severity (High/Med/Low), file:line evidence, suggested fix direction. Cohesion/coupling metrics. Rejected: linear list (loses categorization), weaknesses-only (loses credibility balance). <em>~8-12 pages.</em></p>\n\n<h4>06_IMPROVEMENT_VISION.md — \"Where should it go?\"</h4>\n\n<p><strong>Golden Path: Time-Horizon Roadmap with Difficulty×Impact Estimates (Path A+C)</strong>. Four horizons: Immediate (next release) — MSP exposure, dead code removal, naming unification, ONDAS.md update; Short-term (1-3 releases) — autotune via sim_ferocity.rb, CLI validation, blackbox orni signals, configurator UI; Medium-term — extract orni_flight.c, multi-axis ONDAS, adaptive ferocity, DSP phase detection; Long-term — autonomous perch, flocking, species-specific profiles, actuator abstraction. Each item: rationale (2-3 sentences), difficulty (★ to ★★★★★), impact (★ to ★★★★★), dependencies. Flash budget analysis: estimate bytes for each immediate item. Rejected: capability-based (harder to prioritize), chronological only (loses why). <em>~6-10 pages.</em></p>\n\n<h4>07_SIMULATION.md — \"How do we validate without hardware?\"</h4>\n\n<p><strong>Golden Path: Physics Validation + Tuning Methodology (Path B+C)</strong>. Architecture: all 6 modes documented with example invocations and output interpretations. Physics mapping: table showing sim variable → firmware variable for every physics quantity. Key gap section: sim uses old ONDAS gate (single-channel), firmware uses three-channel — with explicit code comparison and upgrade path. Key findings from sweep: balanced ferocity (F_down≈F_up≈5-6) minimizes pitch amplitude; higher ferocity (&gt;7) narrows ONDAS window but increases oscillation. Tuning methodology: 5-step protocol (sweep→select→flight→compare→prize) with concrete commands. Limitations: no servo dynamics, no sensor noise model, 2D only, old ONDAS model. Rejected: user manual only (loses validation value), theory only (loses practical tuning). <em>~6-8 pages.</em></p>\n\n<h3>Cross-Document Resonance Map</h3>\n\n<pre>\n01_ARCHITECTURE ──\"see 02 for math\"──▶ 02_CONTROL_THEORY\n02_CONTROL_THEORY ──\"parameterized in 03\"──▶ 03_PARAMETER_SPACE\n02_CONTROL_THEORY ──\"validated in 07\"──▶ 07_SIMULATION\n03_PARAMETER_SPACE ──\"gaps documented in 05\"──▶ 05_CRITIQUE\n04_IDENTITY ──\"principles violated in 05\"──▶ 05_CRITIQUE\n05_CRITIQUE ──\"solutions in 06\"──▶ 06_IMPROVEMENT_VISION\n07_SIMULATION ──\"upgrade path in 06\"──▶ 06_IMPROVEMENT_VISION\n</pre>\n\n<h3>Implementation Order for Rubedo</h3>\n\n<p>Documents are not independent. The dependency chain dictates build order:</p>\n\n<ol>\n<li><strong>02_CONTROL_THEORY</strong> — foundational mathematics, all other docs reference it</li>\n<li><strong>03_PARAMETER_SPACE</strong> — depends on 02 for parameter semantics</li>\n<li><strong>01_ARCHITECTURE</strong> — depends on 02 for data flow accuracy</li>\n<li><strong>07_SIMULATION</strong> — depends on 02 for physics mapping</li>\n<li><strong>04_IDENTITY</strong> — depends on 01 for structural identity</li>\n<li><strong>05_CRITIQUE</strong> — depends on all above for evidence gathering</li>\n<li><strong>06_IMPROVEMENT_VISION</strong> — depends on 05 for problem inventory</li>\n<li><strong>00_INDEX</strong> — last, once all documents exist</li>\n</ol>\n\n<p></parameter></p>\n"}, :execution_time=>0.005}, :args=>{:limit=>3}, :execution_time=>0.005}, {:id=>"call_01_aYvRxHMVf2YkrgRXdpm16912", :name=>"task_recall_notes", :result=>{:notes=>[{:id=>11, :content=>"Three-channel breathing-pause architecture in pid.c — PID terms modulate wing-trajectory parameters, not servo offset:\n\nChannel 1: P-term ...", :tags=>"code,ferocity,ondas,pid,architecture,three-channel,breathing-pause", :links=>"src/main/flight/pid.c,src/main/flight/servos.h,src/main/flight/servos.c,src/main/cli/settings.c", :created_at=>"2026-07-29 13:55:53", :score=>11}, {:id=>1, :content=>"OrniFlight: open-source flight control for servo-flapping ornithopters, forked from Betaflight 4.0.6. FORKNAME=orniflight. GPL v3 licensed...", :tags=>"code,structure,overview", :links=>"README.md,Makefile,src/main/flight/", :created_at=>"2026-07-14 01:17:15", :score=>10}, {:id=>27, :content=>"Mixer architecture: mixTable() is the main mixer entry. For ornithopter with USE_ORNI_MIXER_ONLY, motorCount=4, uses mixerOrnithopter[] ta...", :tags=>"code,mixer,servo,architecture,data-flow", :links=>"src/main/flight/mixer.c,src/main/flight/mixer.h,src/main/flight/servos.c,src/main/flight/servos.h", :created_at=>"2026-07-29 19:09:14", :score=>7}, {:id=>12, :content=>"Ferocity wave-shaping in pid.c: `applyFerocityWaveShaping(sinTheta, dMod, iBias)` computes tanh(F·sinθ)/tanh(F). Now accepts 2 additional ...", :tags=>"code,fero