/main/osd/` — OSD elements, any orni-specific\n\n**MSP:**\n- `src/main/msp/msp.c` — protocol, message handlers\n\n**RX:**\n- `src/main/rx/` — receiver protocols\n\n## Phase 2: Architectural Synthesis\n\nFrom the cartography, synthesize key architectural documents:\n\n### 2a. System Architecture Diagram (Mermaid)\n- Component graph: sensors → PID → mixer → servos\n- Data flow: gyro samples → filter cascade → PID → calculateFlappingFromThrottle → servo PWM\n- Three-channel breathing-pause pathway\n- ONDAS wing-phase feedback loop\n\n### 2b. Control Theory Deep Dive\n- The wing ODE: θ̈ = k₀·T_cmd − k₂·ω\n- Ferocity wave-shaping: tanh(F·sinθ)/tanh(F)\n- Three-channel modulation: P-term→k₀, D-term→ferocity, I-term→asymmetry\n- Phase lock: how wing position feeds back into PID timing\n- Glide mode state machine\n- Servo rate limiting and zero-crossing blend zones\n\n### 2c. Parameter Space Map\n- All orni-specific parameters, their ranges, defaults, interactions\n- servoConfig_t fields\n- PID profiles and how they apply to ornithopter axes\n- CLI vs MSP exposure gaps\n\n### 2d. Feature Dependency Web\n- What #defines control what code paths\n- USE_ORNI_MIXER_ONLY cascade\n- What Betaflight features remain reachable vs dead\n\n## Phase 3: Identity & Critique\n\n### 3a. Project Identity Statement\n- What OrniFlight IS: a flapping-wing flight controller derived from Betaflight 4.0.6\n- Core innovations: ONDAS, ferocity wave-shaping, three-channel breathing-pause\n- Design philosophy: PID modulates wing trajectory, not servo offset\n- Target hardware: STM32F3/F4/F7, PWM servos for wing actuation\n- Community: open-source GPLv3, ornithopter enthusiasts/researchers\n\n### 3b. Strengths\n- Elegant wave-shaping mathematics (tanh normalization)\n- Novel control paradigm (trajectory modulation vs moment modulation)\n- Clean separation of flapping physics from stabilization\n- Ferocity per-stroke with blend zones\n- Glide mode integration\n- SSFF (feed-forward) working in parallel with ONDAS\n\n### 3c. Weaknesses & Fragilities\n\nIdentify every:\n- Dead code path that could be removed\n- Commented-out code blocks\n- Inconsistent naming conventions\n- Missing MSP exposure for new features\n- Tight flash budget (99.43%)\n- Untested edge cases (zero throttle transitions, failsafe, etc.)\n- Poorly documented sections\n- Parameter interactions lacking guardrails\n- Hardcoded magic numbers\n\n### 3d. Code Quality Assessment\n- Cohesion: do modules own their data?\n- Coupling: excessive includes, shared globals\n- Error handling: asserts vs graceful degradation\n- Testability: simulation infrastructure (sim_ferocity.rb)\n- Code duplication patterns\n\n## Phase 4: Improvement Vision\n\n### 4a. Immediate (Next Release)\n- Finish MSP exposure for ondas_gain2/gain3\n- Remove remaining dead code\n- Unify glide/ferocity parameter naming\n- Flash budget optimization targets\n\n### 4b. Short-term (1-3 releases)\n- Autotune: automated PID/gain discovery using sim_ferocity.rb\n- CLI parameter validation (interdependent constraints)\n- Blackbox logging enhancement for orni-specific signals\n- Improved failsafe behavior (glide-to-land)\n- Configurator integration (three-channel UI)\n\n### 4c. Medium-term (Architecture)\n- Migrate critical sections from pid.c to dedicated orni_flight.c\n- Abstract wing physics into pluggable airframe models\n- Multi-axis ONDAS (roll stabilization via differential ferocity)\n- Adaptive ferocity based on airspeed estimation\n- DSP-based wing phase detection without hall sensor\n\n### 4d. Long-term (Vision)\n- Autonomous perch/land using glide mode\n- Flocking/swarm support via telemetry mesh\n- Real-time aerodynamic efficiency optimization\n- Species-specific wing profiles as config presets\n- Hardware abstraction for different actuator types (servo, BLDC, SMA)\n\n## Phase 5: Report Assembly\n\nProduce final documents in `magnum_opus/`:\n\n1. **`00_INDEX.md`** — table of contents, reading guide\n2. **`01_ARCHITECTURE.md`** — system