\\"ondas_gain\\\" src/main/cli/settings.c\"},\"execution_time\":0.076},{\"content\":\"\",\"args\":null,\"result\":null},{\"id\":\"call_00_8ZwWn3PUIrkwyk45EXQi3542\",\"name\":\"read_file\",\"result\":{\"content\":\"#include \\\"rx/rx.h\\\"\\n\\nextern mixerMode_e currentMixerMode;\\n\\nPG_REGISTER_WITH_RESET_FN(servoConfig_t, servoConfig, PG_SERVO_CONFIG, 0);\\n\\nvoid pgResetFn_servoConfig(servoConfig_t *servoConfig) {\\n    servoConfig->dev.servoCenterPulse = 1500;\\n    servoConfig->dev.servoPwmRate = 50;\\n    servoConfig->tri...\",\"range\":[54,100],\"execution_time\":0.01},\"args\":{\"range\":[55,100],\"path\":\"src/main/flight/servos.c\"},\"execution_time\":0.01},{\"content\":\"Now I have the complete ONDAS picture. Let me also verify the full D-term section for one more detail:\",\"args\":null,\"result\":null},{\"id\":\"call_00_TRvdnc4i6u0u5xZnyA6E8835\",\"name\":\"read_file\",\"result\":{\"content\":\"            if (cmpTimeUs(currentTimeUs, levelModeStartTimeUs) > CRASH_RECOVERY_DETECTION_DELAY_US) {\\n                detectAndSetCrashRecovery(pidProfile->crash_recovery, axis, currentTimeUs, delta, errorRate);\\n            }\\n#endif\\n\\n            float dMinFactor = 1.0f;\\n#if defined(USE_D_MIN)\\n   ...\",\"range\":[1639,1665],\"execution_time\":0.011},\"args\":{\"path\":\"src/main/flight/pid.c\",\"range\":[1640,1665]},\"execution_time\":0.011}]", :created_at=>"2026-07-14 14:05:47"}
entry {:prompt=>"reflect more deeply about different gains... with good tuning different types of gains where not much better than one good tuned gain... think what they actually mean and if there is a better more clear or even correct formulation", :answer=>"---\n\n## The Three Gains Are One\n\nYou felt it in flight — *\"different types of gains were not much better than one good tuned gain\"* — and the code confirms why.\n\n### What the Three Gains Actually Compute\n\n| Gain | Multiplies | Phase Function | Shape |\n|------|-----------|----------------|-------|\n| `ondas_gain` | P error | `-｜SW｜` | V-shaped, zero at midstroke |\n| `ondas_gain2` | I error | `flapDeriv / tcmd + 1` | 12 Hz oscillating |\n| `ondas_gain3` | D term | `cos(2θ) − 0.5` | W-shaped |\n\nThey are **three different windows on the same underlying 12 Hz wave**, staggered by small phase offsets. One tuned window already gates PID at the right phase. Three just give you three knobs to express the same shape — overfitting with extra degrees of freedom.\n\nSo the question isn't \"how should the three gains differ\" but rather:\n\n### What Is the *Correct* Phase Function?\n\nThe physical answer: **instantaneous aerodynamic authority**.\n\nAt any phase, the wing's ability to produce a control moment is proportional to its velocity. At midstroke (θ=0), velocity is maximum → full authority. At extremities (θ=±π/2), velocity is zero → zero authority. The wing literally can't correct anything when it's stopped at the turnaround.\n\nThis authority is *already computed* in `calculateFlappingFromThrottle`:\n\n```c\nflappingDerivative = shapedDerivative * thetadot;\n// shapedDerivative = fDeriv * cosθ * sech²(fDeriv·sinθ) / tanh(fDeriv)\n// For F=1: simplifies to cosθ. For F=8: concentrated spike at midstroke.\n```\n\nThe normalized authority is simply:\n\n```\nauthority(θ) = |flappingDerivative| / max(|flappingDerivative|)\n             = |shapedDerivative|          ← already [0,1] normalized\n```\n\nAnd here's the key: **ferocity automatically sharpens the authority window**. At F=8, `|shapedDerivative|` is a tight spike — PID is only active right at midstroke where wing velocity is highest. At F=1, it's a broad cosine — PID is active throughout more of the stroke. This coupling is *already physically correct* and requires no extra tuning.\n\n### The Unified Correct Formulation\n\n**One gain, one gate, one rule:**\n\n```\nauthority = |shapedDerivative|                    // [0..1], auto-sharpened by ferocity\ngate = 1.0 - ondas_gain * 0.01 * (1.0 - authority) // gain=0→1.0, gain=100→authority\n\n// P and D: gated by instantaneous authority\nerrorRate *= gate;        // → P goes through gate\ndTermFactor *= gate;      // → D goes through gate\n\n// I: UNGATED — let integrator see all error continuously\n// The integrator is slow; gating it at 12 Hz makes it chase the flap\n```\n\nPlus an optional **feed-forward** (what `ondas_gain2` was trying to be, in the commented-out version):\n\n```\nerrorRate -= flappingDerivative * ff_gain;   // subtract predicted flap artifact\n```\n\nThis removes the known 12 Hz disturbance *before* PID sees it, leaving only the aerodynamic error. Clean signal in → clean PID out.\n\n### Why I-Term Must Be Ungated\n\nThe integrator's job is to accumulate *persistent bias* — e.g., the ornithopter always pitches down due to CG offset. If you gate the I-term input at 12 Hz, it accumulates during mid-stroke and pauses during extremities. Over many strokes, the sign of the accumulation depends on the phase relationship between error and gate — creating a ratcheting bias that drifts with phase. The integrator should integrate. Period.\n\n### The Three→One Mapping\n\n| Old | New |\n|-----|-----|\n| `ondas_gain` (P gate) | → `ondas_gain` (unified gate on P+D) |\n| `ondas_gain2` (I modulation) | → removed (I ungated) + optional `ondas_ff` feed-forward |\n| `ondas_gain3` (D gate) | → same `ondas_gain` as P (same authority function) |\n\nOne gain. One physically-meaningful gate function. I ungated. Optional feed-forward.\n\nShall I implement this?", :tool_call_count=>6, :execution_time=>73.276127, :timestamp=>nil, :tool_calls_json=>"[{\"content\":\"\",\"args\":null,\"result\":null},{\"id\":\"call_00_2zEwNy9Uo2WFTj6dzHDJ3851\",\"name\":\"read_file\",\"result\":{\"content\":\"}\\n\\n\\nvoid feedForwardCorrection(float basePhase) {\\n    float correctionRate = 0.01; // Adjust this value based on tuning\\n    theta = (theta * (1 - correctionRate)) + (basePhase * correctionRate);\\n}\\n\\n\\n\\nstatic inline float ferocityParamToFloat(int8_t param) {\\n    return 1.0f + ((float)(param - 1) * ...\",\"range\":[582,730],\"execution_time\":0.027},\"args\":{\"path\":\"src/main/flight/pid.c\",\"range\":[583,730]},\"execution_time\":0.027},{\"id\":\"call_01_PRx8ocay5f09IfBIRgmo6683\",\"name\":\"read_file\",\"result\":{\"content\":\"#endif\\n        gyroRateDterm[axis] = dtermNotchApplyFn((filter_t *) &dtermNotch[axis], gyroRateDterm[axis]);\\n        gyroRateDterm[axis] = dtermLowpassApplyFn((filter_t *) &dtermLowpass[axis], gyroRateDterm[axis]);\\n        gyroRateDterm[axis] = dtermLowpass2ApplyFn((filter_t *) &dtermLowpass2[axi...\",\"range\":[1499,1665],\"execution_time\":0.022},\"args\":{\"path\":\"src/main/flight/pid.c\",\"range\":[1500,1665]},\"execution_time\":0.022},{\"content\":\"\",\"args\":null,\"result\":null},{\"id\":\"call_00_NqLurgP0JMh11w1CtiYU7453\",\"name\":\"read_file\",\"result\":{\"content\":\"\\nFAST_RAM_ZERO_INIT float throttle_;\\nstatic FAST_RAM_ZERO_INIT float flappingSinusoid;\\nstatic FAST_RAM_ZERO_INIT float flappingSinusoid2;\\nstatic FAST_RAM_ZERO_INIT float flappingCosinusoid;\\nstatic FAST_RAM_ZERO_INIT float flappingAmplitude;\\nFAST_RAM_ZERO_INIT float ornithopterFlapping;\\nstatic FAS...\",\"range\":[85,98],\"execution_time\":0.008},\"args\":{\"path\":\"src/main/flight/pid.c\",\"range\":[86,98]},\"execution_time\":0.008},{\"id\":\"call_01_dhkloD8yVN55FXCWAv2X5134\",\"name\":\"run_command\",\"result\":{\"ok\":true,\"exit_status\":0,\"result\":\"Command output: src/main/cli/settings.c:1429:    { &quot;ondas_gain&quot;,            VAR_INT8 | MASTER_VALUE, .config.minmax = { -100, 100 }, PG_SERVO_CONFIG, offsetof(servoConfig_t, ondas_gain) },\\nsrc/main/cli/settings.c:1430:    { &quot;ondas_gain2&quot;,           VAR_INT8 | MASTER_VALUE, .co...\",\"execution_time\":0.083},\"args\":{\"cmd\":\"grep -rn \\\"ondas_gain\\\" src/main/cli/settings.c\"},\"execution_time\":0.083}]", :created_at=>"2026-07-14 15:39:07"}
entry {:prompt=>"sounds good we are merging new features and simplify old sloppy code", :answer=>"---\n\n## Done — ONDAS Simplified\n\nSix surgical edits collapsed the three-gain ONDAS into a single physically-meaningful authority gate.\n\n### What Changed\n\n| Before | After |\n|--------|-------|\n| `ondasAttenuation = -｜SW｜+0.5` — V-shaped, sign-inverts at gain>10 | `ondasAuthority = ｜shapedDerivative｜` — direct aerodynamic authority |\n| `ondasAttenuationDerivative = cos(2θ)` — separate D window, sign-inverts | Same gate as P — one authority function |\n| `ondas_gain` → P only, `ondas_gain3` → D only | **`ondas_gain` → P+D unified** |\n| `ondas_gain2` → I-term modulated at 12 Hz (broken) | **`ondas_gain2` → feed-forward** (subtracts flap artifact before PID) |\n| I-term gated at flap frequency | **I-term ungated** — integrates cleanly |\n| `* 0.1` scaling → sign flip at gain > 10 | **`* 0.01` scaling** → safe across full [-100,100] |\n| `ondas_gain3` — separate knob | **unused** (D uses same gate as P) |\n\n### The Gate Formula\n\n```\ngate = 1.0 - gain * 0.01 * (1.0 - authority)\n```\n\n| `ondas_gain` | Effect |\n|-------------|--------|\n| 0 | PID sees full error everywhere (off) |\n| 50 | PID fades to 50% at stroke extremes |\n| 100 | PID strictly proportional to instantaneous wing velocity |\n\nFerocity **auto-sharpens** the authority window — no extra tuning needed. F=1 gives a broad cosine; F=8 gives a tight spike right at midstroke where velocity peaks.\n\n### Deleted Dead Weight\n\nRemoved four globals: `ondasAttenuation`, `ondasAttenuationDerivative`, `normalizedFlappingIntegral`, `flappingSinusoid2`. The `applyPhaseShift` function (1e-9 scaling — effectively NOP) is still there but inert; `feedForwardCorrection` is still unused.\n\nReady to compile and test.", :tool_call_count=>37, :execution_time=>196.637382, :timestamp=>nil, :tool_calls_json=>"[{\"content\":\"\",\"args\":null,\"result\":null},{\"id\":\"call_00_p7XkP4enFx9MOU5OOBLx0267\",\"name\":\"rea