lt\":{\"ok\":true,\"execution_time\":0.005},\"args\":{\"id\":9},\"execution_time\":0.005},{\"content\":\"\",\"args\":null,\"result\":null},{\"id\":\"call_00_gIAjp3d1pQtEqIkEYeKa0378\",\"name\":\"aegis\",\"result\":{\"aegis_notes\":[{\"id\":10,\"content\":\"Unified ONDAS architecture in pid.c (simplified from 3-gain to 1-gain + optional feed-forward):\\n\\nSingle authority gate: ondasAuthority = |shapedDerivative| ∈ [0,1]. The shapedDerivative = d/dt[tanh(F·sinθ)/tanh(F)] is already normalized and auto-sharpens with ferocity (F=1→broad cosine, F=8→tight spike at midstroke).\\n\\nGate formula: errorRate *= 1.0 - gain*0.01*(1.0 - authority). gain=0: full PID. gain=100: PID ∝ instantaneous aerodynamic authority. Safe across full [-100,100] CLI range.\\n\\nGain ma...\",\"tags\":\"code,ondas,ferocity,pid,architecture,unified\",\"links\":\"src/main/flight/pid.c,src/main/flight/servos.h,src/main/cli/settings.c\",\"created_at\":\"2026-07-14 16:24:42\",\"score\":42},{\"id\":7,\"content\":\"ONDAS+Ferocity unified architecture in pid.c: Second-order wing ODE θ̈=k₀·T_cmd−k₂·ω drives phase θ. Key state: flappingSinusoid=sinθ, shapedFlappingSinusoid=tanh(F·sinθ)/tanh(F) (ferocity wave-shaped), flappingCosinusoid, flappingDerivative (shaped), ondasAttenuation=-|shapedFlappingSinusoid|+0.5, ondasAttenuationDerivative=cos²θ−sin²θ, normalizedFlappingIntegral, ornithopterFlapping=shapedFlappingSinusoid*amplitude. Ferocity: per-stroke (down/up) via tanh sigmoid, 1.0-8.0 range from int8 param...\",\"tags\":\"code,ondas,ferocity,flapping,pid,architecture\",\"links\":\"src/main/flight/pid.c,src/main/flight/servos.h,src/main/cli/settings.c,ONDAS.md\",\"created_at\":\"2026-07-14 01:38:50\",\"score\":41},{\"id\":6,\"content\":\"Ferocity wave-shaping ported from Gralha Azul to OrniFlight pid.c. New globals: shapedFlappingSinusoid (ferocity-distorted wave). Functions: ferocityParamToFloat() maps int8 1-100 → float 1.0-8.0; applyFerocityWaveShaping(sinTheta) computes tanh(F*sinθ)/tanh(F) with per-stroke ferocity and ±0.1 rad blend zone. calculateFlappingFromThrottle() now: computes flappingSinusoid=sinθ, calls applyFerocityWaveShaping, uses shapedFlappingSinusoid for ondasAttenuation (-|shapedWave|+0.5) and ornithopterFla...\",\"tags\":\"code,ferocity,ondas,architecture\",\"links\":\"src/main/flight/pid.c,src/main/flight/servos.h,src/main/flight/servos.c,src/main/cli/settings.c,ONDAS.md\",\"created_at\":\"2026-07-14 01:38:23\",\"score\":26},{\"id\":8,\"content\":\"Simulation harness at sim_ferocity.rb with 3 modes: wave (static wave shape at given ferocity), flight (full wing ODE + airframe + PID pitch dynamics), sweep (parameter scan over ferocity combinations). Key findings: F=1.0 (pure sine) gives symmetric thrust with minimal pitch disturbance; balanced ferocity (F_down≈F_up≈5-6) minimizes pitch amplitude; higher ferocity (>7) narrows ONDAS window but increases pitch oscillation slightly. Wing ODE: θ̈=k₀·T_cmd−k₂·ω with θ modulo 2π. Airframe: 1st-orde...\",\"tags\":\"simulation,ferocity,ondas,code\",\"links\":\"sim_ferocity.rb,src/main/flight/pid.c\",\"created_at\":\"2026-07-14 02:03:10\",\"score\":25},{\"id\":5,\"content\":\"Gralha Azul (RP2040) ferocity formula in formaDoBaterDasAsas(): shapedWave = tanh(ferocity * sin(θ)) / tanh(ferocity). Ferocity per channel: downstroke (CH7, 1.0-8.0), upstroke (CH8, 1.0-8.0), with linear blend zone ±0.1 rad at zero crossing. Low ferocity → pure sine; high ferocity → near square wave (earlier movement, longer at extreme). Wave always normalized to [-1,+1]. Servo rate limiting in glide: ferocity controls transition speed. Constants: FEROCIDADE_MINIMA_PADRAO=1.0, FEROCIDADE_MAXIMA...\",\"tags\":\"ferocity,code,formula,gralha-azul\",\"links\":\"~~/Users/d/Desktop/HOI_KOSMOI/paraeksperiment/Arduino/libraries/o-grande-codigo-da-gralha-azul/src/GralhaAzul.h~~ (path not found),~~/Users/d/Desktop/HOI_KOSMOI/paraeksperiment/Arduino/libraries/o-grande-codigo-da-gralha-azul/src/GralhaAzul_Padraos.h~~ (path not found)\",\"created_at\":\"2026-07-14 01:34:07\",\"score\":7},{\"id\":1,\"content\":\"OrniFlight: open-source flight control for servo-flapping ornithopters, forked from Betaflight 4.0.6. FORKNAME=orniflight. GPL v3 licensed. Key innovation: ONDAS (Oscillating Normalized Dynamic Adaptive Stabilization) for flapping-wing flight dynamics.\\n\\nProject structure: src/main/ with standard Betaflight layout — flight/, fc/, drivers/, sensors/, io/, cli/, msp/, rx/, osd/, telemetry/, pg/, config/. Build via Makefile targeting STM32F3/F4/F7 MCUs.\",\"tags\":\"code,structure,overview\",\"links\":\"README.md,Makefile,src/main/flight/\",\"created_at\":\"2026-07-14 01:17:15\",\"score\":4}],\"aegis_orientation\":{\"tags\":[\"ondas\",\"ferocity\",\"pid\",\"unified\",\"architecture\"],\"summary\":\"Unified ONDAS: 3 gains collapsed to 1 authority gate + 1 optional feed-forward. I-term ungated. Cleaned dead code (flappingSinusoid2, ondasAttenuat...\",\"temperature\":0.0,\"working_dir\":null,\"thinking\":null},\"execution_time\":0.014},\"args\":{\"summary\":\"Unified ONDAS: 3 gains collapsed to 1 authority gate + 1 optional feed-forward. I-term ungated. Cleaned dead code (flappingSinusoid2, ondasAttenuation, ondasAttenuationDerivative, normalizedFlappingIntegral). ondas_gain3 now unused (D merges with P gate). Safe full-range scaling (*0.01 prevents s...\",\"tags\":[\"ondas\",\"ferocity\",\"pid\",\"unified\",\"architecture\"]},\"execution_time\":0.015},{\"content\":\"\",\"args\":null,\"result\":null},{\"id\":\"call_00_miYxJvecthkStQpjNYnK1085\",\"name\":\"remove_note\",\"result\":{\"ok\":true,\"execution_time\":0.005},\"args\":{\"id\":7},\"execution_time\":0.005}]", :created_at=>"2026-07-14 16:25:03"}
entry {:prompt=>"my ondas attenuation i think was mostly about trying to ignore and filter out the errors introduced by flapping motion... when we apply the pid based on flap cycle we can deal with that... does our system now handle destabilization of pid loop from flapping?", :answer=>"The system has two mechanisms that *should* work together, but the order is currently wrong. Let me trace through it.\n\n### The Two-Layer Defense\n\n```\nLayer 1 — Feed-forward (ondas_gain2):\n  errorRate -= flappingDerivative * gain2 * 0.01\n  → Removes the predicted 12 Hz flap artifact from the raw gyro signal\n  → \"This oscillation is just the wings — don't correct for it\"\n\nLayer 2 — Authority gate (ondas_gain):\n  errorRate *= 1.0 - gain * 0.01 * (1.0 - authority)\n  → Scales corrections by how much wing can actually respond right now\n  → \"The wing is nearly stopped here — any correction would be wasted\"\n```\n\n### The Bug: Gate Before Feed-Forward\n\nThe current code gates **first**, *then* subtracts feed-forward:\n\n```c\n// Gate first:\nerrorRate *= 1.0 - gain*0.01*(1.0 - authority);  // ← scales everything down\n\n// Then feed-forward:\nerrorRate -= flappingDerivative * gain2 * 0.01;  // ← subtracts FULL prediction\n```\n\nConsider the stroke extreme where `authority → 0` and `ondas_gain=100`:\n- Gate zeros `errorRate` → 0\n- Feed-forward then subtracts `flappingDerivative * gain2 * 0.01` from 0\n- **Result: a large negative error at the turnaround**\n- PID tries to correct it — exactly the destabilization you're worried about\n\nMathematically, if the feed-forward prediction were perfect (prediction = flap artifact):\n\n| Phase | Gate→FF (current) | FF→Gate (correct) |\n|-------|-------------------|-------------------|\n| Midstroke (authority=1) | ✅ `disturbance` | ✅ `disturbance` |\n| Extremity (authority=0) | ❌ `−artifact` | ✅ `0` |\n| Partial (authority=0.5) | ⚠️ `0.5×disturbance − 0.5×artifact` | ✅ `0.5×disturbance` |\n\nAt the extremities, the current order actively **injects** the flap artifact back into the error — sign-inverted. The PID then fights it.\n\n### The Fix\n\nSwap two blocks so feed-forward cleans the signal *before* gating. One-line reorder. Shall I apply it?", :tool_call_count=>3, :execution_time=>69.304293, :timestamp=>nil, :tool_calls_json=>"[{\"content\":\"The question deserves careful inspection. Let me verify the current state of both mechanisms — feed-forward and authority gate — are correctly wired together.\",\"args\":null,\"result\":null},{\"id\":\"call_00_i29fyXM0QKV3dZNtQp180637\",\"name\":\"read_file\",\"result\":{\"content\":\"        flappingSinusoid = sin(theta);\\n        flappingCosinusoid = cos(theta);\\n\\n        // Ferocity wave shaping: transform sin(θ) → tanh(F·sinθ)/tanh(F)\\n        applyFerocityWaveShaping(flappingSinusoid);\\n\\n        // Shaped derivative: d/dt[shapedWave] for authority gate and error-rate counteri...\",\"range\":[674,730],\"execution_time\":0.014},\"args\":{\"path\":\"src/main/flight/pid.c\",\"range\":[675,730]},\"execution_time\":0.015},{\"id\":\"call_01_QvIr4DCXVyywNF0teXig9096\",\"name\":\"read_file\",\"result\":{\"content\":\"            // -------- ONDAS unified authority gate -------------------------------\\n            // gate = 1.0 - gain*0.01*(1.0 - authority): only PID at high wing velocity\\n            if (servoConfig()->ondas_gain != 0) {\\n                errorRate *= 1.0f - (1.0f - ondasAuthority) * (float)servo...\",\"range\":[1569,1630],\"execution_time\":0.01},\"args\":{\"path\":\"src/main/flight/pid.c\",\"range\":[1570,1630]},\"execution_time\":0.01}]", :created_at=>"2026-07-15 00:23:34"}
entry {:prompt=>"hi", :answer=>"*The æther stirs.*\n\nGreetings. We stand at a good point — the unified ONDAS gate is in place, and the feed-forward ordering issue is identified and ready for a single swap when you're ready to resume.", :tool_call_count=>0, :execution_time=>4.314739, :timestamp=>nil, :tool_calls_json=>"[]", :created_at=>"2026-07-29 12:16:38"}
entry {:prompt=>"we have made improvements to the flapping algorithm, can you please check and incorporate in here? /Users/d/Desktop/HOI_KOSMOI/paraeksperiment/Arduino/libraries/o-grande-codigo-da-gralha-azul", :answer=>"Now I have the full architecture. Here's my analysis:\n\n---\n\n## Gralha Azul v1.30.30 — What Changed\n\nThe flapping algorithm was **completely rewritten** from tanh-based to **trapezoidal with variable-duration dwell**. This is a bigger change than I initially expected.\n\n### Old (tanh, currently in OrniFlight)\n\n```\nshapedWave = tanh(F·sinθ) / tanh(F)\n```\n- Continuous wave — servo always moving\n- Derivative: smooth sech² bell-curve for ONDAS authority\n- One ferocity per channel (down/up), blended at ±0.1 rad zero-crossing\n\n### New (trapezoidal + dwell, Gralha Azul v1.30.30)\n\n```\nEach half-cycle (descent [0,π), ascent [π,2π)):\n  duration ∝ (8−f)          — softer = longer half-cycle\n  d = f/8                    — dwell fraction [0,1]\n  dh = d/2                   — dwell at each extreme\n\n  t ∈ [0, dh]:       stay at extreme (+1 or −1)    ← DWELL\n  t ∈ [dh, 1−dh]:    cos ramp transition             ← MOVEMENT  \n  t ∈ [1−dh, 1]:     stay at extreme (−1 or +1)    ← DWELL\n  \n  Fast-path f≥7.999: pure square wave (sign of sin)\n```\n\nKey innovations:\n1. **Dwell at extremes** — the servo pauses at top/bottom of stroke. This is physically correct (wings reverse direction) and reduces power at high ferocity by letting the servo hold rather than fight inertia\n2. **Variable half-cycle duration** — asymmetric ferocity shifts the threshold (limiar), giving different stroke ratios\n3. **Fast-path** — at f≥8, skips all float math and returns pure square wave: `θ < π ? 1.0 : −1.0`\n4. **Rudder via differential ferocity + limiar shift** — CH9 differentially biases ferocities in trapezoidal regime and shifts threshold in square regime, with smooth interpolation via `quadFactor`\n\n### Impact on ONDAS\n\nThe derivative shape changes fundamentally. In dwell regions: derivative = 0 → **ONDAS gate fully closes** (authority=0). In ramp regions: derivative is a sine pulse with amplitude ∝ 1/(half-span). This means:\n\n| Ferocity | Dwell | Movement arc | ONDAS window |\n|----------|-------|-------------|--------------|\n| f=0 | 0% | Full cosine 0→π | Broad, low amplitude (same as before) |\n| f=4 | 25% each extreme | 50% of arc | Narrower, sharper spike |\n| f=7 | 43.75% each extreme | 12.5% of arc | Very tight spike at midstroke |\n| f=8 | 50% each extreme | 0% (instant) | Zero everywhere |\n\nThis auto-sharpens the ONDAS window more aggressively than tanh did, matching physical reality better.\n\n### What to Port\n\nI need to replace `applyFerocityWaveShaping` (tanh-based, lines 628-658) with the trapezoidal function, and update the derivative computation in `calculateFlappingFromThrottle`. The SSFF (zero-crossing on raw sin) and unified ONDAS gate structure stay the same.\n\nShall I apply the patch?", :tool_call_count=>28, :execution_time=>198.107986, :timestamp=>nil, :tool_calls_json=>"[{\"content\":\"\",\"args\":null,\"result\":null},{\"id\":\"call_00_Dm81CXbjEcjd30m1GFFO9284\",\"name\":\"run_command\",\"result\":{\"ok\":true,\"exit_status\":0,\"result\":\"Command output: /Users/d/Desktop/HOI_KOSMOI/paraeksperiment/Arduino/libraries/o-grande-codigo-da-gralha-azul/src/GralhaAzul_Padraos.h\\n/Users/d/Desktop/HOI_KOSMOI/paraeksperiment/Arduino/libraries/o-grande-codigo-da-gralha-azul/src/GralhaAzul.h\\n/Users/d/Desktop/HOI_KOSMOI/paraeksperiment/Arduino/l...\",\"execution_time\":0.099},\"args\":{\"cmd\":\"find /Users/d/Desktop/HOI_KOSMOI/paraeksperiment/Arduino/libraries/o-grande-codigo-da-gralha-azul/src -type f -name \\\"*.h\\\" -o -name \\\"*.cpp\\\" -o -name \\\"*.ino\\\" 2>/dev/null | head -30\"},\"execution_time\":0.1},{\"id\":\"call_01_opEiM4b0JbQeb3yLB9F50493\",\"name\":\"run_command\",\"result\":{\"ok\":true,\"exit_status\":0,\"result\":\"Command output: total 160\\ndrwxr-xr-x   5 d  staff    160 Jul 25 12:57 .\\ndrwxr-xr-x  14 d  staff    448 Jul 29 14:53 ..\\n-rw-r--r--   1 d  staff   5145 Jul 25 12:57 GralhaAzul_Padraos.h\\n-rw-r--r--@  1 d  staff    255 Jul  4 14:26 GralhaAzul.cpp\\n-rw-r--r--   1 d  staff  68328 Jul 25 14:32 GralhaAzul...\",\"execution_time\":0.041},\"args\":{\"cmd\":\"ls -la /Users/d/Desktop/HOI_KOSMOI/paraeksperiment/Arduino/libraries/o-grande-codigo-da-gralha-azul/src/\"},\"execution_time\":0.041},{\"content\":\"\",\"args\":null,\"result\":null},{\"id\":\"call_00_G9Qe862BrvRaKp6tEYB51469\",\"name\":\"read_file\",\"result\":{\"error\":\"File not found: /Users/d/Desktop/HOI_KOSMOI/paraeksperiment/OrniFlight/Users/d/Desktop/HOI_KOSMOI/paraeksperiment/Arduino/libraries/o-grande-codigo-da-gralha-azul/src/GralhaAzul_Padraos.h\",\"execution_time\":5.851},\"args\":{\"path\":\"/Users/d/Desktop/HOI_KOSMOI/paraeksperiment/Arduino/libraries/o-grande-codigo-da-gralha-azul/src/GralhaAzul_Padraos.h\"},\"execution_time\":5.852},{\"id\":\"call_01_tZIVBRHc5O9eisma1npf8380\",\"name\":\"read_file\",\"result\":{\"error\":\"File not found: /Users/d/Desktop/HOI_KOSMOI/paraeksperiment/OrniFlight/Users/d/Desktop/HOI_KOSMOI/paraeksperiment/Arduino/libraries/o-grande-codigo-da-gralha-azul/src/GralhaAzul.h\",\"execution_time\":5.447},\"args\":{\"path\":\"/Users/d/Desktop/HOI_KOSMOI/paraeksperiment/Arduino/libraries/o-grande-codigo-da-gralha-azul/src/GralhaAzul.h\"},\"execution_time\":5.447},{\"content\":\"\",\"args\":null,\"result\":null},{\"id\":\"call_00_haQCCRVWMdYnXgdG9V2e8163\",\"name\":\"run_command\",\"result\":{\"ok\":true,\"exit_status\":0,\"result\":\"Command output: 125 /Users/d/Desktop/HOI_KOSMOI/paraeksperiment/Arduino/libraries/o-grande-codigo-da-gralha-azul/src/GralhaAzul_Padraos.h\\n    1385 /Users/d/Desktop/HOI_KOSMOI/paraeksperiment/Arduino/libraries/o-grande-codigo-da-gralha-azul/src/GralhaAzul.h\\n       3 /Users/d/Desktop/HOI_KOSMOI/par...\",\"execution_time\":0.081},\"args\":{\"cmd\":\"wc -l /Users/d/Desktop/HOI_KOSMOI/paraeksperiment/Ardu