[MNEMOSYNE][RECORD]: tool_calls=[{:content=>""}, {:id=>"call_00_80iNzc1swFSpKptfiZiI1060", :name=>"aegis", :result=>{:aegis_notes=>[{:id=>11, :content=>"Three-channel breathing-pause architecture in pid.c — PID terms modulate wing-trajectory parameters, not servo offset:\n\nChannel 1: P-term → phase advance via k0 scaling. \"Push harder now.\" `flappingPhaseModulation = 1.0 + P * ondas_gain * 0.00005`, clamped [0.5, 2.0]. Applied as `k0 * modulation` in wing ODE. Compresses/stretches current ramp.\n\nChannel 2: D-term → ferocity (wave sharpness). \"Delay next opposite stroke.\" `flappingFerocityModulation = D * ondas_gain2 * 0.0003`, clamped [-0.5, 0.5]...", :tags=>"code,ferocity,ondas,pid,architecture,three-channel,breathing-pause", :links=>"src/main/flight/pid.c,src/main/flight/servos.h,src/main/flight/servos.c,src/main/cli/settings.c", :created_at=>"2026-07-29 13:55:53", :score=>59}, {:id=>16, :content=>"Three-channel breathing-pause modulation in pid.c PID loop (PITCH axis only): P-term→phase advance via k0 scaling: flappingPhaseModulation = 1.0 + P * ondas_gain * 0.00005, clamped [0.5, 2.0]. Applied as k0 * modulation in wing ODE. D-term→ferocity wave sharpness: flappingFerocityModulation = D * ondas_gain2 * 0.0003, clamped [-0.5, 0.5]. Applied as dMod in applyFerocityWaveShaping(). I-term→up/down asymmetry: flappingAsymmetryBias = I * ondas_gain3 * 0.0001, clamped [-3.0, 3.0]. Applied as iBia...", :tags=>"code,ferocity,ondas,pid,architecture,three-channel,breathing-pause", :links=>"src/main/flight/pid.c,src/main/flight/servos.h,src/main/cli/settings.c", :created_at=>"2026-07-29 19:08:27", :score=>55}, {:id=>41, :content=>"sim_ferocity.rb: Ruby simulation harness with 6 modes. Uses trapezoidal wave shaping (ported from GralhaAzul / OrniFlight): dwell at ±1 for d/2, cos ramp between. f∈[0,8], d=f/8. param_to_f maps [1,100]→[0,8] matching firmware. Mode wave: static shape analysis. Mode flight: wing ODE + airframe + PID + ONDAS gate + ferocity + SSFF. Mode sweep/compare/derive/prize as before. dshaped_dtheta replaces old tanh deriv_gain.", :tags=>"simulation,ferocity,ondas,code,trapezoidal", :links=>"sim_ferocity.rb,src/main/flight/pid.c", :created_at=>"2026-07-30 01:00:40", :score=>32}, {:id=>39, :content=>"Trapezoidal wave shaping in pid.c applyFerocityWaveShaping(): dwell ratio d = F/8, F ∈ [0,8]. Each half-stroke: dwell at ±1 for d/2 of half-cycle, then cos ramp from ±1 to ∓1 over remaining (1-d)/2. Shared limiar computed from raw config ferocities (not modulated) for both wings to reverse at same instant. Shaped derivative: 0 in dwell, ∓k·sin(k·(t-dh))·dt/dθ·ω in ramp. ferocityParamToFloat: F = (param-1)*8.0/99.0. F=0 → pure cosine, F=8 → pure square via sign(sinθ). FEROCITY_BLEND_ZONE removed.", :tags=>"code,ferocity,ondas,architecture,trapezoidal,wave-shaping", :links=>"src/main/flight/pid.c,src/main/flight/servos.h,src/main/cli/settings.c", :created_at=>"2026-07-30 00:54:45", :score=>27}, {:id=>23, :content=>"PID flow in pidController(): (1) Pre-calc gyro D-term with RPM filter + notch + dual lowpass cascade. (2) Init flapping amplitude via getFlappingAmplitude(throttle_*1000+1000). (3) calculateFlappingFromThrottle(): wing ODE step + ferocity wave shaping, populates ornithopterFlapping/shapedFlappingSinusoid. (4) Per-axis loop: setpoint rate → accel limit → level/horizon modes → acro trainer → launch control → yaw spin recovery → error rate. (5) On PITCH: applyStrokeSynchronousFF(errorRate) → three-...", :tags=>"code,pid,flow,architecture,control-loop", :links=>"src/main/flight/pid.c,src/main/flight/pid.h", :created_at=>"2026-07-29 19:08:50", :score=>25}, {:id=>18, :content=>"SSFF (Stroke-Synchronous Feed-Forward) in pid.c: measures pitch errorRate over each half-stroke, biases next stroke's ferocity. applyStrokeSynchronousFF(pitchErrorRate) called on PITCH axis. Detects sinθ zero crossing: when prevSin * sin <= 0 and they differ → half-stroke boundary. Computes mean error = ssffAccumError/ssffAccumCount. If prevSin > 0 (finished downstroke): ssffFerocityUpBias = ssff_gain * 0.001 * meanError. If prevSin < 0 (finished upstroke): ssffFerocityDownBias = -ssff_gain * 0....", :tags=>"code,ssff,feed-forward,ferocity,pid", :links=>"src/main/flight/pid.c,sim_ferocity.rb,ONDAS.md", :created_at=>"2026-07-29 19:08:27", :score=>23}, {:id=>15, :content=>"Wing ODE in pid.c: θ̈ = k₀·T_cmd − k₂·ω with θ modulo 2π. k₀=1.0, k₂=10.0 (hardcoded globals). T_cmd computed from RC throttle: tcommand = (rc_throttle - 480.0) * ((1.0/(0.1*flap_base_frequency)) + ((flap_speed_modificator - 1500) * 0.000725)). Phase ODE integrated via explicit Euler: θ += ω·dT, ω += ω̇·dT. Flapping derived as sin(θ) then shaped by ferocity wave. When throttle > GLIDE_MODE_THRESHOLD(1040): normal flapping. Below: zero flapping (glide). Flapping amplitude: ((throttle - 1040) * 0....", :tags=>"code,wing-ode,pid,physics,architecture", :links=>"src/main/flight/pid.c,src/main/flight/pid.h,src/main/pg/pg.h", :created_at=>"2026-07-29 19:08:27", :score=>21}, {:id=>38, :content=>"Wave shaping ported from GralhaAzul formaDoBaterDasAsas() to pid.c — trapezoidal model: dwell+f/8+cos ramp, no tanh. applyFerocityWaveShaping(theta, dMod, iBias). Shared limiar from raw config ferocities. ferocityParamToFloat [1,100]→[0,8]. flappingCosinusoid removed. Flash 254,968/252KB.", :tags=>"code,ferocity,trapezoidal,wave-shaping", :links=>"src/main/flight/pid.c", :created_at=>"2026-07-30 00:50:27", :score=>21}], :aegis_orientation=>{:tags=>["ferocity", "ondas", "pid", "architecture", "three-channel", "breathing-pause", "trapezoidal"], :summary=>"Creative exploration: re-conceptualizing flapping wing control nomenclature. Evaluating whether ONDAS survives as umbrella name, how to name the three trajectory-modulation channels, and what new concepts emerge from the PD-blend insight.", :temperature=>1.5, :working_dir=>nil, :thinking=>"max"}, :execution_time=>0.02}, :args=>{:thinking=>"max", :temperature=>1.5, :summary=>"Creative exploration: re-conceptualizing flapping wing control nomenclature. Evaluating whether ONDAS survives as umbrella name, how to name the three trajectory-modulation channels, and what new concepts emerge from the PD-blend insight."}, :execution_time=>0.021}]
